1
00:00:01,492 --> 00:00:03,561
(Let's Go to My House)

2
00:00:03,562 --> 00:00:04,662
Nice to see you all.

3
00:00:06,002 --> 00:00:07,061
It's been a while.

4
00:00:07,062 --> 00:00:08,131
- Nice to see you. - It's been a while.

5
00:00:08,132 --> 00:00:11,031
I heard you found a new place.

6
00:00:11,032 --> 00:00:13,201
Yes. I found a nice house.

7
00:00:13,202 --> 00:00:14,271
- You moved? - Yes.

8
00:00:14,272 --> 00:00:15,571
- Finally. - Yes, finally.

9
00:00:15,572 --> 00:00:16,742
You sound like someone else.

10
00:00:17,042 --> 00:00:18,712
(Chattering)

11
00:00:18,942 --> 00:00:20,642
- Yes, my voice is hoarse. - You...

12
00:00:20,982 --> 00:00:22,652
- Is it because of the World Cup? - Yes.

13
00:00:23,052 --> 00:00:24,351
I was trying to outperform Bae Seong Jae.

14
00:00:24,352 --> 00:00:25,652
(Joking)

15
00:00:26,582 --> 00:00:28,121
- You can't, though. - I can't.

16
00:00:28,122 --> 00:00:29,392
He's an expert.

17
00:00:29,652 --> 00:00:31,422
I don't think you should talk.

18
00:00:31,552 --> 00:00:32,791
I should.

19
00:00:32,792 --> 00:00:35,061
- You found a new place. I should. - That's right.

20
00:00:35,062 --> 00:00:37,231
Or we can keep the conversation going. You can rest.

21
00:00:37,232 --> 00:00:38,432
What should I do then? Dance?

22
00:00:39,632 --> 00:00:41,331
I'll do something at least.

23
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:42,871
(I'll do my share of the work.)

24
00:00:42,872 --> 00:00:44,631
Let's check out his new house.

25
00:00:44,632 --> 00:00:45,702
I can't wait to see it.

26
00:00:46,642 --> 00:00:49,072
(The First Meeting Is Difficult)

27
00:00:50,672 --> 00:00:52,542
"I'm grateful that it's not raining today."

28
00:00:52,642 --> 00:00:53,981
You're still keeping up with your gratitude journal.

29
00:00:53,982 --> 00:00:56,302
I can't believe you're still doing your gratitude journal.

30
00:00:56,552 --> 00:00:57,652
"Before..."

31
00:00:58,612 --> 00:00:59,882
"entering the new house,"

32
00:01:01,282 --> 00:01:02,492
"I should..."

33
00:01:03,422 --> 00:01:04,521
"calm myself down."

34
00:01:04,522 --> 00:01:06,591
(Before entering the new house, I should calm myself down.)

35
00:01:06,592 --> 00:01:08,361
- Is this the moving day? - Yes.

36
00:01:08,362 --> 00:01:10,662
I won't be able to see the green leaves anymore.

37
00:01:11,662 --> 00:01:14,022
I'm moving out of my old place where I lived for two years.

38
00:01:14,502 --> 00:01:17,431
I found a new home for myself.

39
00:01:17,432 --> 00:01:19,302
- So I'm moving today. - You're moving today.

40
00:01:19,972 --> 00:01:22,742
(Last time, he looked into loans to move to a new place.)

41
00:01:23,372 --> 00:01:26,181
(Kang Yong excitedly checked out different houses.)

42
00:01:26,182 --> 00:01:27,182
You know what?

43
00:01:27,183 --> 00:01:29,111
(You can't act all excited in front of realtors.)

44
00:01:29,112 --> 00:01:30,911
Right. He was so excited in front of the realtors back then.

45
00:01:30,912 --> 00:01:34,022
(Hyun Moo lectured him out of concern for him.)

46
00:01:35,752 --> 00:01:36,752
(Knocking)

47
00:01:36,753 --> 00:01:39,261
(This is nice.)

48
00:01:39,262 --> 00:01:40,592
(What's nice about it?)

49
00:01:41,062 --> 00:01:42,961
(Gosh, the elevator is opening.)

50
00:01:42,962 --> 00:01:44,322
- Of course. - All elevators open.

51
00:01:44,432 --> 00:01:46,701
- It'd be weird if they didn't. - I dreamed of having an elevator.

52
00:01:46,702 --> 00:01:48,678
(Kang Yong, do you think you can find a new place?)

53
00:01:48,702 --> 00:01:49,871
After that day,

54
00:01:49,872 --> 00:01:52,471
I visited four more real estate agencies.

55
00:01:52,472 --> 00:01:55,042
I looked at ten more houses.

56
00:01:55,512 --> 00:01:57,041
(Kang Yong found a new place after all his effort.)

57
00:01:57,042 --> 00:01:58,271
You lived there for two years.

58
00:01:58,272 --> 00:02:00,342
Yes. I matured my lease before I moved out.

59
00:02:00,582 --> 00:02:02,281
I have time.

60
00:02:02,282 --> 00:02:03,962
(He writes his journal on the moving day.)

61
00:02:04,952 --> 00:02:07,482
(But he hasn't packed his things in the bathroom yet.)

62
00:02:07,652 --> 00:02:09,021
(His belongings haven't been packed either.)

63
00:02:09,022 --> 00:02:10,091
- It's your moving day. - It's your...

64
00:02:10,092 --> 00:02:11,151
- moving day. - You haven't packed anything.

65
00:02:11,152 --> 00:02:12,961
(There's a pile of things to take care of.)

66
00:02:12,962 --> 00:02:14,192
You didn't pack anything yet.

67
00:02:16,862 --> 00:02:18,031
"The new house..."

68
00:02:18,032 --> 00:02:19,712
You shouldn't be writing your journal now.

69
00:02:21,862 --> 00:02:24,702
This is my last day here.

70
00:02:25,402 --> 00:02:28,742
(I should start packing now.)

71
00:02:28,872 --> 00:02:29,912
First of all,

72
00:02:31,572 --> 00:02:33,442
I should start with my clothes.

73
00:02:35,012 --> 00:02:37,382
I've already moved about ten times.

74
00:02:37,912 --> 00:02:39,881
I think it won't take long to move.

75
00:02:39,882 --> 00:02:42,692
Actually, I know some tips about packing up my things.

76
00:02:42,822 --> 00:02:46,262
Besides, going up and down three flights of stairs is nothing.

77
00:02:46,592 --> 00:02:49,332
I'm still young. So it won't be a problem.

78
00:02:50,032 --> 00:02:53,202
(Kang Yong feels confident about packing.)

79
00:02:54,332 --> 00:02:57,131
(Messily rolling his clothes)

80
00:02:57,132 --> 00:02:59,348
If you roll them like that, you can't pack a lot of clothes.

81
00:02:59,372 --> 00:03:01,402
- Right. - You can't pack a lot of clothes.

82
00:03:01,702 --> 00:03:02,871
(Startled)

83
00:03:02,872 --> 00:03:04,712
I thought an old guy was joining us.

84
00:03:05,412 --> 00:03:08,042
It's like he traveled 20 years into the future.

85
00:03:08,412 --> 00:03:10,212
Hyun Moo, it must be your voice.

86
00:03:10,652 --> 00:03:12,282
You sound really wise.

87
00:03:12,782 --> 00:03:15,122
- It's like... - It's like an elder is talking.

88
00:03:15,182 --> 00:03:17,791
You know the master in the movie, "Kung Fu Panda?"

89
00:03:17,792 --> 00:03:19,562
- You sound more trustworthy. - That's good.

90
00:03:19,922 --> 00:03:22,661
- My words are wise. - It's like he's enlightened.

91
00:03:22,662 --> 00:03:24,462
- It's like we shouldn't oppose him. - Right.

92
00:03:25,032 --> 00:03:26,631
(Kang Yong is still packing his things.)

93
00:03:26,632 --> 00:03:28,162
(Ringing)

94
00:03:30,832 --> 00:03:32,441
"I just confirmed that your deposit has been returned."

95
00:03:32,442 --> 00:03:33,542
Okay.

96
00:03:34,842 --> 00:03:36,012
You got it back.

97
00:03:36,672 --> 00:03:38,372
I just have to move into my new place.

98
00:03:40,282 --> 00:03:42,852
- You must've been excited. - I bet it was fun.

99
00:03:43,212 --> 00:03:44,582
Moving days are exciting.

100
00:03:45,682 --> 00:03:47,121
I got this from my senior.

101
00:03:47,122 --> 00:03:48,751
(I have memories about this book.)

102
00:03:48,752 --> 00:03:51,122
I should bring it for the decor.

103
00:03:52,152 --> 00:03:53,261
It's right here.

104
00:03:53,262 --> 00:03:54,262
(Finding another item of nostalgia)

105
00:03:54,263 --> 00:03:55,462
I found the pedals.

106
00:03:56,492 --> 00:03:57,832
You had a piano?

107
00:03:58,062 --> 00:03:59,431
I tried to take up the piano during COVID-19...

108
00:03:59,432 --> 00:04:01,202
because we weren't allowed to gather.

109
00:04:01,762 --> 00:04:03,631
I only played it once. After that...

110
00:04:03,632 --> 00:04:05,532
- You're just like me. - Right.

111
00:04:07,342 --> 00:04:09,611
I had it in the storage for six years.

112
00:04:09,612 --> 00:04:10,671
I was trying to sell it through an app,

113
00:04:10,672 --> 00:04:11,832
but I didn't have the pedals.

114
00:04:11,912 --> 00:04:13,411
- I posted it, but couldn't sell it. - You didn't have the pedals either.

115
00:04:13,412 --> 00:04:14,712
Are you your role model?

116
00:04:15,542 --> 00:04:16,812
I found them on the moving day.

117
00:04:19,522 --> 00:04:22,491
"MBC Basic Work Competency Assessment."

118
00:04:22,492 --> 00:04:23,622
Gosh, this is crazy.

119
00:04:24,892 --> 00:04:26,922
I studied to get into MBC in this house.

120
00:04:27,692 --> 00:04:29,261
I have a lot of memories studying to get into MBC there.

121
00:04:29,262 --> 00:04:31,732
So I won't be able to forget that house.

122
00:04:32,262 --> 00:04:34,931
Luckily, your two years in the house have been all good.

123
00:04:34,932 --> 00:04:35,972
Right.

124
00:04:36,172 --> 00:04:37,401
The house must have good energy.

125
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:38,402
- Right. - Some houses have good energy.

126
00:04:38,403 --> 00:04:39,472
I shouldn't.

127
00:04:41,142 --> 00:04:43,342
Will it work?

128
00:04:44,172 --> 00:04:45,941
(He gets a call when he's packing up.)

129
00:04:45,942 --> 00:04:48,111
- Hello. - Hello.

130
00:04:48,112 --> 00:04:49,551
- Hi. - Yes.

131
00:04:49,552 --> 00:04:50,581
This is the cleaning crew captain.

132
00:04:50,582 --> 00:04:51,582
- The cleaning crew? - Yes.

133
00:04:51,583 --> 00:04:54,151
- Do you know the passcode? - Right.

134
00:04:54,152 --> 00:04:55,581
I'll give you the passcode. Wait.

135
00:04:55,582 --> 00:04:57,792
Were you able to get in?

136
00:04:58,192 --> 00:04:59,192
No. Because we couldn't get in...

137
00:04:59,193 --> 00:05:01,591
He just asked you for the passcode.

138
00:05:01,592 --> 00:05:02,962
I was all over the place that day.

139
00:05:03,432 --> 00:05:05,761
You don't want the home appliances like the fridge...

140
00:05:05,762 --> 00:05:07,832
or the washing machine to be cleaned, right?

141
00:05:08,162 --> 00:05:09,932
I thought it was included in the package.

142
00:05:10,532 --> 00:05:12,271
- No, it's charged separately. - Is that so?

143
00:05:12,272 --> 00:05:13,371
- That would cost extra. - Then...

144
00:05:13,372 --> 00:05:15,571
- Right. - Then you don't have to clean them.

145
00:05:15,572 --> 00:05:17,071
Okay. I got it.

146
00:05:17,072 --> 00:05:18,642
Call me if you need anything else.

147
00:05:18,742 --> 00:05:19,781
- Okay. - Okay.

148
00:05:19,782 --> 00:05:21,862
(He finishes the phone call with the cleaning crew.)

149
00:05:22,682 --> 00:05:25,182
(He gets another call.)

150
00:05:26,452 --> 00:05:27,582
Hello, sir.

151
00:05:27,922 --> 00:05:29,992
- Hello. - Hello.

152
00:05:30,392 --> 00:05:31,591
- I'm on my way. - Yes.

153
00:05:31,592 --> 00:05:33,521
It looks like I'll arrive...

154
00:05:33,522 --> 00:05:35,221
- I called a mover. - at 2:05pm.

155
00:05:35,222 --> 00:05:36,761
- I see. - I'll see you in a bit.

156
00:05:36,762 --> 00:05:37,932
Okay.

157
00:05:38,062 --> 00:05:39,932
I'm almost done.

158
00:05:40,262 --> 00:05:43,202
Why did I buy this? I barely played it. Seriously.

159
00:05:43,532 --> 00:05:45,212
I should take it with me. What could I do?

160
00:05:45,942 --> 00:05:47,172
Give it to Hue.

161
00:05:48,502 --> 00:05:49,812
The keyboard was working.

162
00:05:50,272 --> 00:05:51,712
Sell all the keyboards to Hue.

163
00:05:52,072 --> 00:05:53,141
All right.

164
00:05:53,142 --> 00:05:54,862
(I should take this big table with me too.)

165
00:05:55,182 --> 00:05:57,311
It's amazing that we always end up with more things.

166
00:05:57,312 --> 00:05:58,981
I didn't know I had that much stuff in the balcony.

167
00:05:58,982 --> 00:06:00,481
If you didn't use them there,

168
00:06:00,482 --> 00:06:01,881
you wouldn't use them for the next two years either.

169
00:06:01,882 --> 00:06:02,921
- Right. - That's so true.

170
00:06:02,922 --> 00:06:04,551
- I haven't touched them yet. - I bet.

171
00:06:04,552 --> 00:06:06,361
- Once you don't, you never do. - Never.

172
00:06:06,362 --> 00:06:08,262
(Gosh, that old guy...)

173
00:06:08,522 --> 00:06:12,031
(He's in front of the shoe closet.)

174
00:06:12,032 --> 00:06:14,161
- Will they fit? - He has a lot of stuff.

175
00:06:14,162 --> 00:06:16,082
- He's got a lot of shoes. - I need to be smart.

176
00:06:16,502 --> 00:06:19,572
I saw this tip on social media.

177
00:06:19,742 --> 00:06:23,241
They said packing shoes in a suitcase made things easier.

178
00:06:23,242 --> 00:06:24,911
- Boxes would've been better. - Right.

179
00:06:24,912 --> 00:06:25,912
- Or just plastic bags. - Yes.

180
00:06:25,913 --> 00:06:27,313
I could fit only eight pairs in it.

181
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:29,712
- It's so inefficient. - It is.

182
00:06:31,412 --> 00:06:33,822
(He busily packs his things in the bathroom.)

183
00:06:34,922 --> 00:06:36,221
(A pile of kitchen items)

184
00:06:36,222 --> 00:06:38,121
- You have so much stuff. - The kitchen... The shelves...

185
00:06:38,122 --> 00:06:39,492
You have so much stuff.

186
00:06:40,062 --> 00:06:41,462
Why do I have so much stuff?

187
00:06:44,092 --> 00:06:45,262
There's no end.

188
00:06:45,962 --> 00:06:48,462
Why do you have so much stuff? What do you do in the house?

189
00:06:49,672 --> 00:06:50,772
He's here.

190
00:06:51,832 --> 00:06:52,872
Hello.

191
00:06:53,772 --> 00:06:54,772
- Hey. - Yes.

192
00:06:54,773 --> 00:06:56,211
- I'm downstairs. - Yes.

193
00:06:56,212 --> 00:06:58,411
But the thing is, I'm not done...

194
00:06:58,412 --> 00:07:00,012
- packing my things yet. - I see.

195
00:07:00,482 --> 00:07:01,541
We can do it together.

196
00:07:01,542 --> 00:07:04,181
- Okay. - Could you come down for a second?

197
00:07:04,182 --> 00:07:05,281
- I see. - Okay.

198
00:07:05,282 --> 00:07:06,582
They pack things really fast.

199
00:07:08,252 --> 00:07:09,292
My gosh.

200
00:07:09,922 --> 00:07:12,352
(Rushing)

201
00:07:13,262 --> 00:07:15,592
- Hello. - Hello.

202
00:07:18,462 --> 00:07:19,462
(The mover has arrived.)

203
00:07:19,463 --> 00:07:21,131
I bet he's really good at his job.

204
00:07:21,132 --> 00:07:22,772
- He's got toned muscles. Right? - Yes.

205
00:07:25,232 --> 00:07:29,672
(He climbs up 3 flights of stairs with the mover to his unit.)

206
00:07:30,442 --> 00:07:32,641
- So you're moving everything here. - That's right.

207
00:07:32,642 --> 00:07:33,911
- Then... - I boxed up some things.

208
00:07:33,912 --> 00:07:36,081
- let's load the boxes... - Yes.

209
00:07:36,082 --> 00:07:37,951
- you already packed. - Okay.

210
00:07:37,952 --> 00:07:41,951
- After that, let's use my boxes... - Okay.

211
00:07:41,952 --> 00:07:43,821
- to pack the rest. - Oh, we're using your boxes?

212
00:07:43,822 --> 00:07:45,351
- Of course. - Thank you.

213
00:07:45,352 --> 00:07:47,661
Today was the first time I got help from the movers...

214
00:07:47,662 --> 00:07:49,331
to pack my things.

215
00:07:49,332 --> 00:07:51,892
The package with partial packing assistance was quite expensive.

216
00:07:52,262 --> 00:07:53,362
It cost 170 dollars.

217
00:07:53,562 --> 00:07:57,372
It costs as much as a month's rent at my new place.

218
00:07:57,732 --> 00:08:00,771
So I wanted to save up as much money as possible.

219
00:08:00,772 --> 00:08:03,942
And I'm young and strong too.

220
00:08:04,742 --> 00:08:06,181
I only needed partial assistance to pack.

221
00:08:06,182 --> 00:08:07,641
I mean, I'm healthy too.

222
00:08:07,642 --> 00:08:08,782
I believed in my abilities.

223
00:08:09,912 --> 00:08:11,381
I thought it'd be too much to do it on my own.

224
00:08:11,382 --> 00:08:13,528
But I thought getting the partial package would be okay.

225
00:08:13,552 --> 00:08:14,752
You did it on your own before?

226
00:08:15,082 --> 00:08:18,151
I did everything on my own. I even rented a truck.

227
00:08:18,152 --> 00:08:19,291
You're so frugal.

228
00:08:19,292 --> 00:08:20,522
(How frugal he is.)

229
00:08:20,862 --> 00:08:21,962
Thank you.

230
00:08:22,632 --> 00:08:23,912
- This old man approves. - Okay.

231
00:08:24,832 --> 00:08:25,932
You're frugal.

232
00:08:26,132 --> 00:08:27,301
Let's start with this box.

233
00:08:27,302 --> 00:08:30,002
- I'll carry these two. - Okay.

234
00:08:30,132 --> 00:08:31,301
- You see those boxes you packed? - Okay.

235
00:08:31,302 --> 00:08:33,302
- Bring them one at a time. - One? Okay.

236
00:08:35,302 --> 00:08:38,442
Those boxes aren't light at all.

237
00:08:38,972 --> 00:08:40,711
His grip is different.

238
00:08:40,712 --> 00:08:42,088
Right. And he crossed the boxes too.

239
00:08:42,112 --> 00:08:43,552
- He knows what to do. - Yes.

240
00:08:44,912 --> 00:08:46,021
(This young and strong guy will begin too.)

241
00:08:46,022 --> 00:08:47,152
Yes, show us what you got.

242
00:08:48,282 --> 00:08:49,822
Gosh, this is so heavy.

243
00:08:51,492 --> 00:08:53,262
(Trying again)

244
00:08:53,692 --> 00:08:55,592
(Inhaling sharply)

245
00:08:57,332 --> 00:08:58,462
You have no idea what to do.

246
00:09:00,932 --> 00:09:02,202
It was really heavy.

247
00:09:03,172 --> 00:09:04,302
Gosh, it's the heaviest one.

248
00:09:08,172 --> 00:09:09,241
You said you were young.

249
00:09:09,242 --> 00:09:11,012
I'm young and strong too.

250
00:09:11,272 --> 00:09:12,882
Do you miss your youth?

251
00:09:13,542 --> 00:09:14,881
I used to be young once.

252
00:09:14,882 --> 00:09:17,212
(Teary-eyed)

253
00:09:18,282 --> 00:09:19,752
(Exhaling)

254
00:09:21,452 --> 00:09:22,481
It's heavy, right?

255
00:09:22,482 --> 00:09:24,191
You can just put that on the truck.

256
00:09:24,192 --> 00:09:25,321
How do you carry two at once?

257
00:09:25,322 --> 00:09:27,092
He dropped them off and is already going up.

258
00:09:28,762 --> 00:09:31,392
(Struggling)

259
00:09:35,162 --> 00:09:36,471
(He moves one box laboriously.)

260
00:09:36,472 --> 00:09:37,572
He just moved one box.

261
00:09:41,942 --> 00:09:43,741
(Lifting two boxes again)

262
00:09:43,742 --> 00:09:45,772
- They were so heavy. - Just put that...

263
00:09:46,112 --> 00:09:48,281
- Okay. - on the floor on the side.

264
00:09:48,282 --> 00:09:50,182
(Securing the path for the mover's safety)

265
00:09:50,652 --> 00:09:53,222
(He's amazing.)

266
00:09:53,552 --> 00:09:54,552
(Breathing hard)

267
00:09:55,552 --> 00:09:56,552
(Sighing)

268
00:09:57,292 --> 00:09:58,791
(He's exhausted after moving one box.)

269
00:09:58,792 --> 00:10:00,672
Why are you so tired after moving only one box?

270
00:10:01,522 --> 00:10:04,362
I used a lot of my energy beforehand to pack my things.

271
00:10:04,632 --> 00:10:06,401
- You're stalling. - Right.

272
00:10:06,402 --> 00:10:08,061
(Scolding)

273
00:10:08,062 --> 00:10:10,531
He rolled up his sleeves five times.

274
00:10:10,532 --> 00:10:11,671
He didn't grab the box in one go.

275
00:10:11,672 --> 00:10:13,001
"My gosh. This is heavy."

276
00:10:13,002 --> 00:10:15,341
- He keeps complaining. - He's taking too long.

277
00:10:15,342 --> 00:10:17,141
If you keep stalling like that,

278
00:10:17,142 --> 00:10:19,072
movers would comment on that.

279
00:10:19,312 --> 00:10:22,112
A long time ago, an old guy helped me move.

280
00:10:22,342 --> 00:10:24,682
He said, "Are you trying to get this old man to pass out?"

281
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:26,752
He kept saying that.

282
00:10:27,122 --> 00:10:28,552
He kept scolding me like that.

283
00:10:28,952 --> 00:10:32,052
(While he's regrouping to roll up his sleeves, )

284
00:10:32,492 --> 00:10:35,562
(the mover comes back quickly.)

285
00:10:36,232 --> 00:10:38,132
(Startled)

286
00:10:39,262 --> 00:10:41,502
(Lifting)

287
00:10:42,002 --> 00:10:44,172
Let's go. I can do this.

288
00:10:45,072 --> 00:10:46,202
There you go.

289
00:10:47,072 --> 00:10:48,171
You got this.

290
00:10:48,172 --> 00:10:50,011
I felt bad that I only carried one box down.

291
00:10:50,012 --> 00:10:51,411
- So I tried carrying two. - Right.

292
00:10:51,412 --> 00:10:52,512
Yes.

293
00:10:53,412 --> 00:10:55,812
I've got to do this.

294
00:10:56,352 --> 00:10:57,512
Let's go.

295
00:10:58,452 --> 00:11:00,322
(Exhaling)

296
00:11:02,022 --> 00:11:03,291
It would've been harder...

297
00:11:03,292 --> 00:11:04,572
- without the elevator. - Right.

298
00:11:05,492 --> 00:11:06,861
If there had been an elevator,

299
00:11:06,862 --> 00:11:08,191
- you could've just put them in it. - Right.

300
00:11:08,192 --> 00:11:09,291
(Sweating profusely after going up and down the stairs)

301
00:11:09,292 --> 00:11:11,092
Your whole body is going to ache after this.

302
00:11:13,362 --> 00:11:15,162
(Pulling up)

303
00:11:15,932 --> 00:11:17,472
- This is heavy. - Okay.

304
00:11:19,072 --> 00:11:20,141
Gosh, he just...

305
00:11:20,142 --> 00:11:21,372
Seriously.

306
00:11:22,242 --> 00:11:23,811
It looked so light in his hands.

307
00:11:23,812 --> 00:11:25,072
(Surprised)

308
00:11:27,082 --> 00:11:28,212
This is tough, isn't it?

309
00:11:29,312 --> 00:11:32,611
Not having an elevator is huge.

310
00:11:32,612 --> 00:11:34,051
(Panting)

311
00:11:34,052 --> 00:11:37,651
Before packing, it doesn't look like you have a lot of stuff.

312
00:11:37,652 --> 00:11:38,851
Seriously.

313
00:11:38,852 --> 00:11:41,061
Once you start packing, there's no end. It's always like that.

314
00:11:41,062 --> 00:11:42,592
It's like that for everyone, right?

315
00:11:43,192 --> 00:11:44,872
- Other people... - He overtook Kang Yong.

316
00:11:45,532 --> 00:11:47,231
It's hard to overtake someone on stairs.

317
00:11:47,232 --> 00:11:48,932
(Impressed)

318
00:11:49,602 --> 00:11:52,232
Let's bring down one box each.

319
00:11:53,372 --> 00:11:54,571
(He follows his lead and carries the box.)

320
00:11:54,572 --> 00:11:56,142
He told me what to do.

321
00:11:59,642 --> 00:12:01,041
(He's carrying two boxes at once.)

322
00:12:01,042 --> 00:12:02,281
My gosh. That's...

323
00:12:02,282 --> 00:12:03,712
(He's carrying two boxes at once.)

324
00:12:04,552 --> 00:12:05,882
I would've given up moving...

325
00:12:06,822 --> 00:12:08,522
without his help.

326
00:12:09,052 --> 00:12:11,333
He had to keep going up and down three flights of stairs.

327
00:12:11,752 --> 00:12:14,222
Carrying one box was heavy enough.

328
00:12:14,792 --> 00:12:17,192
But he carried two boxes on his back.

329
00:12:17,562 --> 00:12:18,732
He was like the Almighty.

330
00:12:18,832 --> 00:12:20,232
He came to save me.

331
00:12:20,432 --> 00:12:21,802
He got things done so fast.

332
00:12:23,032 --> 00:12:25,071
I choked up a bit. I was incredibly grateful.

333
00:12:25,072 --> 00:12:26,572
(I choked up out of gratitude.)

334
00:12:28,342 --> 00:12:33,042
(He's working hard with every ounce of his energy just like the mover.)

335
00:12:34,642 --> 00:12:37,211
Thinking of the old days when I did everything on my own...

336
00:12:37,212 --> 00:12:38,812
made me realize how reckless I had been.

337
00:12:39,352 --> 00:12:40,552
I can't do this alone now.

338
00:12:42,922 --> 00:12:44,992
(Lifting hard)

339
00:12:46,822 --> 00:12:47,822
(The truck is full.)

340
00:12:47,823 --> 00:12:49,091
Gosh, the truck is full.

341
00:12:49,092 --> 00:12:50,192
You have a lot of stuff.

342
00:12:51,062 --> 00:12:54,462
(Soaked in sweat)

343
00:12:56,672 --> 00:12:58,972
(Grabbing)

344
00:12:59,272 --> 00:13:00,941
(Packing up the empty bottles)

345
00:13:00,942 --> 00:13:02,071
Why are you taking the bottles?

346
00:13:02,072 --> 00:13:04,241
They're bottles of expensive wine.

347
00:13:04,242 --> 00:13:06,012
I took them home after work get-togethers.

348
00:13:06,342 --> 00:13:07,582
I wanted to use them for decor.

349
00:13:08,112 --> 00:13:09,682
They're valuable.

350
00:13:09,912 --> 00:13:11,752
- For home decor? - I put them in my car. Yes.

351
00:13:12,082 --> 00:13:15,152
Your new place will get cluttered pretty fast if you take them all.

352
00:13:15,322 --> 00:13:17,351
It's odd. But you can't help...

353
00:13:17,352 --> 00:13:19,391
but bring all of your things when you move.

354
00:13:19,392 --> 00:13:20,691
They looked valuable to me.

355
00:13:20,692 --> 00:13:22,562
I might find use for them in the new house.

356
00:13:22,692 --> 00:13:24,391
- But you wouldn't notice them gone. - Right.

357
00:13:24,392 --> 00:13:26,631
- Someone should get rid of them. - But you wouldn't notice that.

358
00:13:26,632 --> 00:13:27,731
(He's indeed experienced.)

359
00:13:27,732 --> 00:13:29,412
- His wisdom is on another level. - Right.

360
00:13:29,902 --> 00:13:31,201
- I've gone through everything. - That...

361
00:13:31,202 --> 00:13:32,562
(Just wait until you turn my age.)

362
00:13:33,702 --> 00:13:35,041
(Carefully storing the empty bottles in his car)

363
00:13:35,042 --> 00:13:36,312
The empty bottles...

364
00:13:37,072 --> 00:13:38,312
I want to throw them out.

365
00:13:38,712 --> 00:13:41,712
Hey, take the empty bottles to the district office.

366
00:13:42,682 --> 00:13:45,012
(You're going to my new place, not the district office.)

367
00:13:46,652 --> 00:13:47,921
This is a lot now that we loaded everything, right?

368
00:13:47,922 --> 00:13:49,082
This is a lot of stuff.

369
00:13:50,152 --> 00:13:52,021
- That's all my stuff. - That is a lot of stuff.

370
00:13:52,022 --> 00:13:53,262
You do have a lot of stuff.

371
00:13:53,492 --> 00:13:54,821
- I didn't know it'd be that much. - You do have a lot of things.

372
00:13:54,822 --> 00:13:55,921
You do.

373
00:13:55,922 --> 00:13:58,061
- I have to buy some trash bags... - Okay.

374
00:13:58,062 --> 00:13:59,661
- and clean the house. - Okay.

375
00:13:59,662 --> 00:14:01,501
- Take your time driving there. - Okay.

376
00:14:01,502 --> 00:14:03,431
- I'll text you the passcode. - Okay.

377
00:14:03,432 --> 00:14:05,801
- Please rest until I get there. - Okay.

378
00:14:05,802 --> 00:14:07,101
- Then let's move them together. - Sure.

379
00:14:07,102 --> 00:14:08,422
- I'll try to clean fast. - Okay.

380
00:14:08,542 --> 00:14:11,188
But if you get there a bit late, he'll have moved everything by then.

381
00:14:11,212 --> 00:14:12,241
That's why I told him many times...

382
00:14:12,242 --> 00:14:13,882
- not to do that. - Right.

383
00:14:14,342 --> 00:14:16,012
(Laughing)

384
00:14:17,712 --> 00:14:21,022
(He comes back home to clean up one last time.)

385
00:14:21,522 --> 00:14:23,292
(Grabbing)

386
00:14:24,952 --> 00:14:27,992
(Messy)

387
00:14:29,422 --> 00:14:32,592
(Let's clean up quickly.)

388
00:14:34,862 --> 00:14:37,301
(He's doing the final sweep of the house.)

389
00:14:37,302 --> 00:14:38,332
Gosh, my back hurts.

390
00:14:42,502 --> 00:14:45,042
I don't even know how I got through packing everything.

391
00:14:46,442 --> 00:14:47,442
(Lifting)

392
00:14:47,443 --> 00:14:48,712
It must feel a bit sad.

393
00:14:50,712 --> 00:14:51,912
Right here.

394
00:14:53,822 --> 00:14:56,592
- It's 3.79 dollars. - Okay.

395
00:14:56,722 --> 00:15:00,792
- He came to check the gas meter. - To settle the bill.

396
00:15:01,322 --> 00:15:04,032
They calculate the meter on the moving day for the bill.

397
00:15:04,192 --> 00:15:05,862
- He came for the payment. - I see.

398
00:15:08,032 --> 00:15:10,572
I got the deposit.

399
00:15:11,002 --> 00:15:13,942
Now, I have to settle the balance.

400
00:15:14,342 --> 00:15:16,072
I got the deposit back...

401
00:15:16,342 --> 00:15:18,172
and wired it to the landlord of my new place.

402
00:15:18,412 --> 00:15:19,811
Isn't that a bit sad?

403
00:15:19,812 --> 00:15:20,981
- Right. - It's not your money.

404
00:15:20,982 --> 00:15:22,481
It only passes through your bank account.

405
00:15:22,482 --> 00:15:24,482
It passes through. It was just there for a second.

406
00:15:25,782 --> 00:15:26,881
There are so many things to do...

407
00:15:26,882 --> 00:15:28,221
- when you move. - There were more things to handle.

408
00:15:28,222 --> 00:15:29,452
(A busy moving day)

409
00:15:30,022 --> 00:15:32,251
- Hey. - I'll throw them out and go.

410
00:15:32,252 --> 00:15:33,521
- Did the truck leave? - Pardon?

411
00:15:33,522 --> 00:15:34,592
Did the truck leave?

412
00:15:34,892 --> 00:15:37,192
He's the landlord. He lives upstairs.

413
00:15:37,362 --> 00:15:40,262
- I see. He lives upstairs? - Yes, he does.

414
00:15:41,732 --> 00:15:43,631
(The landlord came down to say goodbye.)

415
00:15:43,632 --> 00:15:45,031
The balcony was always like that.

416
00:15:45,032 --> 00:15:46,071
Did anything break?

417
00:15:46,072 --> 00:15:47,341
- No. - Nothing?

418
00:15:47,342 --> 00:15:49,541
This is a clock from my company.

419
00:15:49,542 --> 00:15:50,671
- A clock? - Yes.

420
00:15:50,672 --> 00:15:52,541
- That's... - That was good.

421
00:15:52,542 --> 00:15:54,242
It's a modern clock.

422
00:15:54,512 --> 00:15:55,811
It's for you. It's from MBC.

423
00:15:55,812 --> 00:15:58,852
- It's a silent clock. - Thank you.

424
00:15:59,012 --> 00:16:01,682
- Sure. It's for you. - The house...

425
00:16:02,052 --> 00:16:04,492
- I'll throw them out and go. - Okay.

426
00:16:05,852 --> 00:16:06,962
Take care.

427
00:16:07,892 --> 00:16:08,992
I'm leaving.

428
00:16:10,032 --> 00:16:11,162
Bye.

429
00:16:12,092 --> 00:16:14,461
- All right. Let's go. - He must feel happy and sad.

430
00:16:14,462 --> 00:16:16,401
It looks like he's ready to move on.

431
00:16:16,402 --> 00:16:18,001
People usually take a long look around...

432
00:16:18,002 --> 00:16:19,571
- before leaving. Right? - That's true.

433
00:16:19,572 --> 00:16:20,672
He came back.

434
00:16:21,542 --> 00:16:22,542
- Leaving right away like that... - Right.

435
00:16:22,543 --> 00:16:24,142
Made me feel a bit sad.

436
00:16:24,342 --> 00:16:25,911
- Of course, it's sad. - Exactly.

437
00:16:25,912 --> 00:16:28,012
- I'd never be able to come back. - Right.

438
00:16:30,312 --> 00:16:34,322
(Kang Yong looks around the house one more time.)

439
00:16:38,822 --> 00:16:40,521
Gosh, it was such a strange feeling.

440
00:16:40,522 --> 00:16:41,862
- Earlier today, - Bye.

441
00:16:42,222 --> 00:16:45,562
The house looked smaller without my things in there.

442
00:16:46,702 --> 00:16:49,261
With my things inside, the house looked bigger.

443
00:16:49,262 --> 00:16:51,472
But without them, the house looked...

444
00:16:52,502 --> 00:16:55,202
I mean, I lived my life...

445
00:16:55,372 --> 00:16:57,042
in this small, precious house.

446
00:16:57,412 --> 00:17:00,282
I practiced for the job interview and commentating on sports games.

447
00:17:00,842 --> 00:17:03,552
I ate and exercised in there. I did all kinds of things.

448
00:17:03,952 --> 00:17:05,812
I had become attached to the house.

449
00:17:14,962 --> 00:17:16,662
I'd think about this house a lot.

450
00:17:17,662 --> 00:17:21,162
It was the first house I had gotten this attached to.

451
00:17:21,362 --> 00:17:22,462
I mean it.

452
00:17:24,102 --> 00:17:25,902
Goodbye, my lover.

453
00:17:27,672 --> 00:17:30,012
(Checking the fridge)

454
00:17:31,442 --> 00:17:32,972
(Tapping)

455
00:17:33,842 --> 00:17:34,912
I'm leaving.

456
00:17:36,812 --> 00:17:38,752
I had a good life here. Let me take a selfie.

457
00:17:51,462 --> 00:17:52,462
I'm going.

458
00:17:53,532 --> 00:17:55,761
Goodbye. Take care.

459
00:17:55,762 --> 00:17:57,871
(I'm going. Goodbye.)

460
00:17:57,872 --> 00:17:58,902
Well done.

461
00:18:04,142 --> 00:18:08,242
(Taking one last photo of the building)

462
00:18:10,512 --> 00:18:11,711
Let's get going.

463
00:18:11,712 --> 00:18:12,751
(He heads to his new place now.)

464
00:18:12,752 --> 00:18:15,582
This is really my last time here now.

465
00:18:16,952 --> 00:18:19,992
My gosh. It's my last day here. I won't come back here.

466
00:18:20,562 --> 00:18:22,462
Take care. Bye.

467
00:18:24,162 --> 00:18:26,632
(He starts humming as soon as he leaves his old house.)

468
00:18:27,102 --> 00:18:28,201
You'd forget the old place by the evening...

469
00:18:28,202 --> 00:18:29,302
as if it were a dream...

470
00:18:29,602 --> 00:18:31,271
- Right. - once you get to the new place.

471
00:18:31,272 --> 00:18:33,201
- That's so true. - That's how we are.

472
00:18:33,202 --> 00:18:34,642
- You'd completely forget it. - Yes.

473
00:18:34,672 --> 00:18:38,112
Great. I'll be living in Gangnam.

474
00:18:38,212 --> 00:18:39,981
- Gangnam? - Gangnam?

475
00:18:39,982 --> 00:18:41,422
I mean it as the south of the river.

476
00:18:41,682 --> 00:18:44,002
- Then Mokpo is Gangnam too. - Yes. That'd be Gangnam too.

477
00:18:45,182 --> 00:18:46,521
- That's true. - I'm going to my new place...

478
00:18:46,522 --> 00:18:47,822
which is near my work.

479
00:18:49,782 --> 00:18:52,752
I'm almost there.

480
00:18:53,562 --> 00:18:54,991
"Mok-dong Apartment."

481
00:18:54,992 --> 00:18:56,422
(His destination is Mok-dong?)

482
00:18:56,792 --> 00:18:58,262
I'm heading to Yangcheon-gu.

483
00:18:59,162 --> 00:19:00,202
Turn here.

484
00:19:01,102 --> 00:19:02,462
Hello, kids.

485
00:19:03,672 --> 00:19:05,472
I'll be your neighbor.

486
00:19:06,002 --> 00:19:07,002
Great.

487
00:19:07,003 --> 00:19:08,241
(He arrives with excitement.)

488
00:19:08,242 --> 00:19:09,912
He's already here.

489
00:19:14,112 --> 00:19:15,681
The mover is already at the new place.

490
00:19:15,682 --> 00:19:18,352
(This is great.)

491
00:19:23,492 --> 00:19:25,192
I'm living near Sinmokdong Station.

492
00:19:25,892 --> 00:19:27,172
It's super close to the station.

493
00:19:27,222 --> 00:19:30,262
I can be at work in 10 to 15 minutes if there's no traffic by car.

494
00:19:30,432 --> 00:19:33,332
Given the distance, the accessibility to work is great.

495
00:19:33,402 --> 00:19:35,762
And the Han River is near my house.

496
00:19:35,932 --> 00:19:38,172
I can easily go for a jog and exercise there.

497
00:19:38,532 --> 00:19:40,402
It's a great place with everything nearby.

498
00:19:43,712 --> 00:19:44,712
Instant rice.

499
00:19:45,842 --> 00:19:47,342
And cash. Let's see.

500
00:19:48,042 --> 00:19:49,042
Okay.

501
00:19:49,043 --> 00:19:50,251
(Okay. Let's go.)

502
00:19:50,252 --> 00:19:51,552
Let's go.

503
00:19:52,512 --> 00:19:54,251
Gosh, there's an elevator.

504
00:19:54,252 --> 00:19:55,352
I love it.

505
00:19:56,522 --> 00:19:57,751
There's an elevator.

506
00:19:57,752 --> 00:20:00,022
(There's an elevator in the building.)

507
00:20:00,892 --> 00:20:02,592
(His heart is full.)

508
00:20:03,732 --> 00:20:06,832
(He quickly gets into the elevator he's grateful for.)

509
00:20:07,302 --> 00:20:08,962
I should enter with cash.

510
00:20:09,132 --> 00:20:13,942
(He gets ready to enter the new home with instant rice.)

511
00:20:14,072 --> 00:20:15,102
Is this the unit?

512
00:20:15,802 --> 00:20:16,812
Okay.

513
00:20:18,472 --> 00:20:20,182
(Opening)

514
00:20:20,742 --> 00:20:22,382
I should bring in the instant rice first.

515
00:20:23,412 --> 00:20:24,451
All good.

516
00:20:24,452 --> 00:20:27,621
(I should bring in the instant rice first.)

517
00:20:27,622 --> 00:20:29,322
Why did you toss in the rice?

518
00:20:29,422 --> 00:20:30,622
When you move to a new place,

519
00:20:31,022 --> 00:20:32,551
you carry a rice cooker inside first...

520
00:20:32,552 --> 00:20:33,861
- Right. - for good luck.

521
00:20:33,862 --> 00:20:36,932
But I didn't have a rice cooker. So I replaced it with instant rice.

522
00:20:37,032 --> 00:20:38,891
I was told to bring in makgeolli first.

523
00:20:38,892 --> 00:20:39,961
I guess it's different.

524
00:20:39,962 --> 00:20:41,602
People bring in makgeolli or red beans.

525
00:20:41,662 --> 00:20:42,942
- Right. - To drive out spirits?

526
00:20:43,532 --> 00:20:45,131
(He finally walks into his new place.)

527
00:20:45,132 --> 00:20:46,232
Gosh, it smells...

528
00:20:50,842 --> 00:20:51,842
(A clean new home for Kang Yong)

529
00:20:51,843 --> 00:20:53,172
It looks nice and neat.

530
00:20:53,942 --> 00:20:55,042
It's well-lit too.

531
00:20:55,982 --> 00:20:57,382
It's a one-bedroom studio.

532
00:20:57,452 --> 00:20:59,052
It's so spacious.

533
00:21:00,282 --> 00:21:02,551
(Even his bathroom is quite big.)

534
00:21:02,552 --> 00:21:04,351
I love having a window in the bathroom.

535
00:21:04,352 --> 00:21:05,821
It helps remove moisture.

536
00:21:05,822 --> 00:21:06,892
Windows are essential.

537
00:21:07,892 --> 00:21:10,162
I like that there's a washing machine.

538
00:21:13,132 --> 00:21:14,501
- I see. This is... - Oh, I see.

539
00:21:14,502 --> 00:21:15,908
- There's a balcony. - This is nice.

540
00:21:15,932 --> 00:21:18,231
This was a major deciding factor in choosing this place.

541
00:21:18,232 --> 00:21:20,078
- There's an outdoor balcony. - A balcony. Right.

542
00:21:20,102 --> 00:21:21,401
I don't want to go out for drinks.

543
00:21:21,402 --> 00:21:24,112
I can have beer or wine alone out in the balcony.

544
00:21:24,612 --> 00:21:25,872
I can look at the view.

545
00:21:26,412 --> 00:21:28,711
The balconies are often the deciding factor for many people.

546
00:21:28,712 --> 00:21:30,212
- But people rarely use it. - Right.

547
00:21:30,612 --> 00:21:32,381
- They'd never go out there. - I didn't use it once after moving.

548
00:21:32,382 --> 00:21:34,951
Besides, it doesn't have a roof.

549
00:21:34,952 --> 00:21:37,222
- You have one more place to clean. - Right.

550
00:21:37,292 --> 00:21:39,491
The balcony will get caked with dirt.

551
00:21:39,492 --> 00:21:41,021
- Dirt comes in when you open it. - Right.

552
00:21:41,022 --> 00:21:42,761
It's too small for you to sit out there.

553
00:21:42,762 --> 00:21:44,722
You'll probably go out there fewer than 30 times.

554
00:21:44,962 --> 00:21:46,831
- I was going to... - But the view is unobstructed.

555
00:21:46,832 --> 00:21:48,312
- Right. - The view is great, though.

556
00:21:49,302 --> 00:21:50,471
(Checking out the bedroom instead of the unobstructed view)

557
00:21:50,472 --> 00:21:53,002
I can't believe I have a bed. This is crazy.

558
00:21:53,972 --> 00:21:55,741
Gosh, there's a closet too.

559
00:21:55,742 --> 00:21:57,222
(But the house is already furnished.)

560
00:21:57,472 --> 00:22:00,082
I'm really grateful. The previous tenant...

561
00:22:00,482 --> 00:22:03,381
left the bed, the closet, the table in the living room,

562
00:22:03,382 --> 00:22:06,551
and the computer desk.

563
00:22:06,552 --> 00:22:07,582
For free?

564
00:22:07,722 --> 00:22:09,382
I saved up a lot of money.

565
00:22:09,422 --> 00:22:11,198
- I said I'd be happy to take them. - That's great.

566
00:22:11,222 --> 00:22:13,322
The security deposit is 200,000 dollars.

567
00:22:14,062 --> 00:22:16,782
The monthly rent is 150 dollars. It's a partial deposit-based house.

568
00:22:16,862 --> 00:22:19,492
I got a 100,000-dollar loan from a bank.

569
00:22:19,632 --> 00:22:22,432
I took out a 20,000-dollar loan from my company.

570
00:22:22,532 --> 00:22:24,272
So my loans are 120,000 dollars.

571
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:28,602
I pay 290 dollars every month to the bank for the loan.

572
00:22:28,772 --> 00:22:30,612
As for the loan from my company,

573
00:22:31,072 --> 00:22:32,772
I'm amortizing it.

574
00:22:33,242 --> 00:22:35,441
I have to pay back about 600 dollars every month.

575
00:22:35,442 --> 00:22:38,811
So I'm paying 900 dollars every month.

576
00:22:38,812 --> 00:22:41,093
- That's a lot of money. - That's how much I pay a month.

577
00:22:41,222 --> 00:22:42,782
Nine hundred dollars is a hefty amount.

578
00:22:43,052 --> 00:22:45,552
Seriously. That kind of money for office workers...

579
00:22:45,652 --> 00:22:47,652
- It's not easy. - He has to be on a tight budget.

580
00:22:48,022 --> 00:22:50,291
What about your car? Any expenses there?

581
00:22:50,292 --> 00:22:51,861
- It was a used car. - I see.

582
00:22:51,862 --> 00:22:53,861
- You bought it with cash. - I only have to cover...

583
00:22:53,862 --> 00:22:54,902
- the gas for it. - I see.

584
00:22:54,962 --> 00:22:56,701
After two years,

585
00:22:56,702 --> 00:22:59,272
I can lower the interest rate of the loan...

586
00:22:59,302 --> 00:23:00,742
from my company.

587
00:23:00,902 --> 00:23:03,301
So I'll wait two years...

588
00:23:03,302 --> 00:23:05,422
and then change it to another plan with a lower rate.

589
00:23:05,542 --> 00:23:06,782
So I can reduce my expenses.

590
00:23:07,212 --> 00:23:10,112
So I'm paying 900 dollars...

591
00:23:10,352 --> 00:23:11,812
every month.

592
00:23:11,912 --> 00:23:14,822
Including the rent, I have to pay 1,050 dollars.

593
00:23:15,822 --> 00:23:16,922
The prices...

594
00:23:18,392 --> 00:23:20,292
at the MBC cafeteria are very reasonable.

595
00:23:21,122 --> 00:23:23,392
My plan is to save up a lot of money now.

596
00:23:24,132 --> 00:23:26,532
So I can take it easy later. With that in mind,

597
00:23:26,802 --> 00:23:28,902
I came up with this financial plan.

598
00:23:29,202 --> 00:23:30,948
I bet you'll basically live in the cafeteria.

599
00:23:30,972 --> 00:23:33,002
I had breakfast at the cafeteria.

600
00:23:33,972 --> 00:23:36,471
When I have a big expense coming up, I try to cut back...

601
00:23:36,472 --> 00:23:38,772
- on food. That's my first move. - Right.

602
00:23:39,272 --> 00:23:40,992
Not getting delivery food would help a lot.

603
00:23:41,112 --> 00:23:42,818
- Right. - One delivery fee is equivalent...

604
00:23:42,842 --> 00:23:45,182
- to three meals in the cafeteria. - Right.

605
00:23:45,612 --> 00:23:48,722
This was my first time taking out loans.

606
00:23:48,952 --> 00:23:51,112
Since it's a large sum of money, it doesn't feel real.

607
00:23:52,092 --> 00:23:54,091
But I knew I could find ways to save money.

608
00:23:54,092 --> 00:23:55,261
Right. We all find ways...

609
00:23:55,262 --> 00:23:56,862
- to make it work. - You'll pay it back.

610
00:23:57,192 --> 00:24:00,461
It feels weird to take out a loan...

611
00:24:00,462 --> 00:24:03,031
- for the 1st time. - Right. It was my 1st time.

612
00:24:03,032 --> 00:24:04,752
- It makes you feel like an adult. - Right.

613
00:24:04,932 --> 00:24:06,402
And pride comes into play too.

614
00:24:06,532 --> 00:24:08,401
When they have to check your credit score...

615
00:24:08,402 --> 00:24:10,342
- Right. - "Come on."

616
00:24:10,642 --> 00:24:11,742
"Don't you read webtoons?"

617
00:24:12,642 --> 00:24:14,002
I said that once when I was young.

618
00:24:14,082 --> 00:24:16,281
They said they couldn't give me a big loan.

619
00:24:16,282 --> 00:24:17,311
(The memory of his first loan is like a scene in a webtoon.)

620
00:24:17,312 --> 00:24:18,812
- Right. - It's a pride thing.

621
00:24:19,882 --> 00:24:21,622
That's right.

622
00:24:22,022 --> 00:24:24,792
(He checks if the water is running just for the sake of it.)

623
00:24:25,952 --> 00:24:27,161
It's clean.

624
00:24:27,162 --> 00:24:29,962
(Satisfied with his clean new home)

625
00:24:31,262 --> 00:24:32,461
I'm late.

626
00:24:32,462 --> 00:24:35,062
(He quickly goes down to the 1st floor to get his things.)

627
00:24:36,132 --> 00:24:37,132
(Rushing)

628
00:24:37,132 --> 00:24:38,132
Sir.

629
00:24:38,133 --> 00:24:40,131
- Get the mirror over there. - What should I grab? The mirror?

630
00:24:40,132 --> 00:24:41,418
- Should I put it on there? - Yes.

631
00:24:41,442 --> 00:24:43,812
- No. To the elevator. - Bring it to the elevator?

632
00:24:46,442 --> 00:24:47,841
- It's not big. - This...

633
00:24:47,842 --> 00:24:50,452
(They take the elevator instead of the stairs this time.)

634
00:24:50,552 --> 00:24:52,251
(His things are moved quickly.)

635
00:24:52,252 --> 00:24:53,852
- It must be much easier. - That's good.

636
00:24:54,122 --> 00:24:55,982
We only needed a quarter of the time...

637
00:24:56,852 --> 00:24:58,422
we spent before.

638
00:25:00,052 --> 00:25:01,092
One.

639
00:25:01,322 --> 00:25:02,882
How many trips do you think we'll need?

640
00:25:02,922 --> 00:25:04,331
- About five trips. - Five?

641
00:25:04,332 --> 00:25:05,762
- Five to six. - I see.

642
00:25:06,462 --> 00:25:08,342
I should always live in a building with stairs.

643
00:25:08,862 --> 00:25:10,702
I mean, with an elevator.

644
00:25:12,902 --> 00:25:13,971
(He's clearly in love with his new home.)

645
00:25:13,972 --> 00:25:16,002
Wait a moment.

646
00:25:17,342 --> 00:25:19,141
Gosh, he should make good use of the elevator.

647
00:25:19,142 --> 00:25:20,222
(Moving his things quickly)

648
00:25:22,112 --> 00:25:24,952
I'm so grateful to the inventor of elevators.

649
00:25:25,352 --> 00:25:26,582
We really should be.

650
00:25:27,422 --> 00:25:29,251
The AC is on in the elevator too.

651
00:25:29,252 --> 00:25:30,321
(Gratefully arriving at his unit)

652
00:25:30,322 --> 00:25:31,391
One, two, three.

653
00:25:31,392 --> 00:25:33,392
(Moving in his things one at a time)

654
00:25:35,122 --> 00:25:36,691
It's not too hard with the elevator. Right?

655
00:25:36,692 --> 00:25:38,432
Yes. It's easier with the elevator.

656
00:25:39,732 --> 00:25:42,532
(Thanks to the elevator, they can move big boxes quickly.)

657
00:25:43,162 --> 00:25:44,202
- One. - One, two.

658
00:25:45,402 --> 00:25:46,402
There you go.

659
00:25:46,403 --> 00:25:48,003
(They bring in the boxes one at a time.)

660
00:25:48,842 --> 00:25:50,612
Gosh, you have so much stuff.

661
00:25:50,712 --> 00:25:51,871
That was what I had after I had thrown out a lot.

662
00:25:51,872 --> 00:25:54,482
(Stacking them up around the house)

663
00:25:55,682 --> 00:25:56,912
(Placing Wilson down)

664
00:25:57,612 --> 00:25:59,012
- We're done. - We're done.

665
00:25:59,382 --> 00:26:00,681
(They're done moving the boxes at last.)

666
00:26:00,682 --> 00:26:02,122
- Good job. - Thank you.

667
00:26:02,822 --> 00:26:03,991
- I'll go down with you. - Okay.

668
00:26:03,992 --> 00:26:05,091
(They're done moving the boxes at last.)

669
00:26:05,092 --> 00:26:07,091
Having an elevator definitely helps.

670
00:26:07,092 --> 00:26:09,262
- It's convenient. - It's super convenient. I love it.

671
00:26:11,792 --> 00:26:13,432
How much do I owe you?

672
00:26:13,762 --> 00:26:15,461
- It's 170 dollars. - It's 170 dollars.

673
00:26:15,462 --> 00:26:17,071
- I brought cash. - My gosh.

674
00:26:17,072 --> 00:26:18,831
(Hold on.)

675
00:26:18,832 --> 00:26:20,102
Give him extra.

676
00:26:20,302 --> 00:26:22,141
I'm so grateful for your help. I added 50 dollars more.

677
00:26:22,142 --> 00:26:24,441
- That was nice of you. - My old place had no elevator.

678
00:26:24,442 --> 00:26:26,672
You needed to give him extra. That's good.

679
00:26:26,812 --> 00:26:27,942
- Thank you. - Sure.

680
00:26:28,442 --> 00:26:30,281
There was no way I could have done this alone.

681
00:26:30,282 --> 00:26:31,522
(Thinking about it scares him.)

682
00:26:33,722 --> 00:26:35,351
- We got everything, right? - We did.

683
00:26:35,352 --> 00:26:36,382
- Thank you. - Sure.

684
00:26:36,722 --> 00:26:38,321
Take care.

685
00:26:38,322 --> 00:26:39,421
- Bye. - Bye.

686
00:26:39,422 --> 00:26:40,561
- I'll spot you. - Okay.

687
00:26:40,562 --> 00:26:42,021
- Okay. Bye. - I'm so grateful to him too.

688
00:26:42,022 --> 00:26:44,303
He told me to call him if I get married and have to move.

689
00:26:45,862 --> 00:26:47,762
(Trudging)

690
00:26:48,462 --> 00:26:49,832
There is so much stuff.

691
00:26:51,432 --> 00:26:52,572
How will you live there?

692
00:26:54,642 --> 00:26:57,171
(They can't believe their eyes.)

693
00:26:57,172 --> 00:26:58,712
- Oh, no. - My goodness.

694
00:26:59,142 --> 00:27:00,302
- What's that? - My goodness.

695
00:27:00,771 --> 00:27:02,170
(Kang Yong enters his new place.)

696
00:27:02,171 --> 00:27:03,571
There is so much stuff.

697
00:27:08,111 --> 00:27:09,481
- Oh, no. - My goodness.

698
00:27:10,211 --> 00:27:11,310
- What's that? - My goodness.

699
00:27:11,311 --> 00:27:13,481
- Hey, that's... - I was so surprised.

700
00:27:13,711 --> 00:27:14,881
How will you live there?

701
00:27:15,921 --> 00:27:17,851
(There are four chairs...)

702
00:27:18,421 --> 00:27:21,060
(and three tables.)

703
00:27:21,061 --> 00:27:23,691
It's not like you need them for firewood.

704
00:27:24,431 --> 00:27:25,631
Why did you leave them behind?

705
00:27:26,161 --> 00:27:27,361
Lie down on the top.

706
00:27:28,731 --> 00:27:29,930
(Comfortable)

707
00:27:29,931 --> 00:27:31,570
I didn't know that there would be so much stuff.

708
00:27:31,571 --> 00:27:34,301
(There is a lot of stuff.)

709
00:27:36,041 --> 00:27:38,940
(He turns away from the piled-up items.)

710
00:27:38,941 --> 00:27:40,041
(Sighing)

711
00:27:41,981 --> 00:27:43,841
It's already 5:12pm.

712
00:27:45,781 --> 00:27:47,111
I need to hurry.

713
00:27:48,281 --> 00:27:50,050
(He hurriedly goes out without unpacking.)

714
00:27:50,051 --> 00:27:52,051
(Hurried)

715
00:27:52,851 --> 00:27:54,161
I turn to the left.

716
00:27:55,491 --> 00:27:56,961
Seventeen minutes. Okay.

717
00:27:57,961 --> 00:28:00,491
There is a convenience store nearby.

718
00:28:01,761 --> 00:28:03,331
There is a laundromat too.

719
00:28:05,101 --> 00:28:06,370
There is a Chinese restaurant too.

720
00:28:06,371 --> 00:28:08,611
(He checks the infrastructure despite being in a hurry.)

721
00:28:08,841 --> 00:28:11,910
(He arrives at a place at a fast pace.)

722
00:28:11,911 --> 00:28:12,991
(Community service center?)

723
00:28:14,641 --> 00:28:15,910
I wanted to get things done on my day off...

724
00:28:15,911 --> 00:28:17,180
since it was open until 6pm.

725
00:28:17,181 --> 00:28:20,210
To report my date of confirmation and change of address,

726
00:28:20,211 --> 00:28:21,680
I went there hurriedly before it closed.

727
00:28:21,681 --> 00:28:23,681
You need to do that quickly when you pay rent.

728
00:28:23,921 --> 00:28:25,620
Yes, I heard that I needed to do it on the same day...

729
00:28:25,621 --> 00:28:27,290
in order to secure...

730
00:28:27,291 --> 00:28:28,420
- the Preferential Repayment Right. - Yes.

731
00:28:28,421 --> 00:28:30,091
- I see. - It could be a rental scam.

732
00:28:32,531 --> 00:28:34,900
(He gets his queue ticket and waits.)

733
00:28:34,901 --> 00:28:36,531
(Ringing)

734
00:28:37,101 --> 00:28:38,170
(Rushing over)

735
00:28:38,171 --> 00:28:39,500
- Hello. - Hello.

736
00:28:39,501 --> 00:28:42,301
- I moved in today, - Okay.

737
00:28:42,441 --> 00:28:43,470
So I need to report my date of confirmation...

738
00:28:43,471 --> 00:28:45,340
- and change of address. - Right.

739
00:28:45,341 --> 00:28:46,940
- Please give me your ID... - Okay.

740
00:28:46,941 --> 00:28:48,281
- and your contract. - Okay.

741
00:28:48,581 --> 00:28:50,310
Do you need all ten pages?

742
00:28:50,311 --> 00:28:51,510
That moment is a bit nerve-racking.

743
00:28:51,511 --> 00:28:54,520
You feel like you've prepared something wrong.

744
00:28:54,521 --> 00:28:55,521
That's right.

745
00:28:55,522 --> 00:28:56,550
- Is this enough? - Yes.

746
00:28:56,551 --> 00:28:58,120
- This is enough. - Okay.

747
00:28:58,121 --> 00:28:59,667
(He hands over the contract he has brought.)

748
00:28:59,691 --> 00:29:01,990
Please fill out the application form.

749
00:29:01,991 --> 00:29:03,021
Okay.

750
00:29:03,491 --> 00:29:04,760
(Change of address)

751
00:29:04,761 --> 00:29:05,860
(With excitement in his heart, he writes each letter neatly.)

752
00:29:05,861 --> 00:29:07,421
Will you be a resident of Yangcheon-gu?

753
00:29:08,031 --> 00:29:09,900
Is it your first time moving into Yangcheon-gu?

754
00:29:09,901 --> 00:29:11,530
- Yes, it's my first time. - In that case,

755
00:29:11,531 --> 00:29:13,770
we give a welcome gift to people who have moved in...

756
00:29:13,771 --> 00:29:15,700
- from other districts. - Really?

757
00:29:15,701 --> 00:29:16,701
(I see.)

758
00:29:16,702 --> 00:29:18,740
It's a thank you for moving into the district.

759
00:29:18,741 --> 00:29:19,770
- Yes. - That's right.

760
00:29:19,771 --> 00:29:21,911
"Please keep living here without going anywhere."

761
00:29:22,241 --> 00:29:23,241
Okay.

762
00:29:24,111 --> 00:29:25,310
I'll pick this gift.

763
00:29:25,311 --> 00:29:26,591
(Laundry detergent is the best.)

764
00:29:27,051 --> 00:29:28,251
Here you go. Thank you.

765
00:29:29,451 --> 00:29:30,750
Will you add another item to the house?

766
00:29:30,751 --> 00:29:32,021
You have too many items.

767
00:29:32,691 --> 00:29:33,931
I picked the laundry detergent.

768
00:29:34,421 --> 00:29:35,890
I thought about picking the tool set,

769
00:29:35,891 --> 00:29:37,360
but I didn't want to crowd the house further.

770
00:29:37,361 --> 00:29:39,031
Hey, you should've picked the tool set.

771
00:29:39,461 --> 00:29:40,531
Well done.

772
00:29:40,561 --> 00:29:42,201
(It's 100 percent handy.)

773
00:29:44,831 --> 00:29:46,800
- The change of address is complete. - Thank you.

774
00:29:46,801 --> 00:29:48,571
- Here is your new address. - Okay.

775
00:29:49,041 --> 00:29:50,640
And here is your welcome gift.

776
00:29:50,641 --> 00:29:52,670
Thank you.

777
00:29:52,671 --> 00:29:53,911
- Congratulations. - Thank you.

778
00:29:54,941 --> 00:29:55,980
Here it is.

779
00:29:55,981 --> 00:29:59,411
(Feeling excited, he moves to get a copy of resident registration.)

780
00:30:00,551 --> 00:30:01,650
(Happy)

781
00:30:01,651 --> 00:30:02,897
Are you getting a copy for the sake of it?

782
00:30:02,921 --> 00:30:05,050
I wanted to check if the change of address...

783
00:30:05,051 --> 00:30:06,951
had been made successfully.

784
00:30:08,021 --> 00:30:09,060
(Nervous)

785
00:30:09,061 --> 00:30:11,761
(Dropping)

786
00:30:13,731 --> 00:30:16,231
Address, Jungang-ro, Mok-dong, Yangcheon-gu.

787
00:30:16,831 --> 00:30:18,600
- Complete. - In the morning, it was Jung-gu.

788
00:30:18,601 --> 00:30:20,270
In the afternoon, it changed to Yangcheon-gu.

789
00:30:20,271 --> 00:30:22,101
You're a Yangcheon-gu resident now.

790
00:30:24,471 --> 00:30:26,071
What's that? They're selling fruits.

791
00:30:27,911 --> 00:30:29,840
(He heads over to the store to taste Yangcheon-gu's fruits.)

792
00:30:29,841 --> 00:30:31,180
Hello.

793
00:30:31,181 --> 00:30:32,411
- Welcome. - Hello.

794
00:30:34,251 --> 00:30:35,520
- Seon Min... - That place...

795
00:30:35,521 --> 00:30:37,181
went to that vegetable place.

796
00:30:39,121 --> 00:30:41,960
(A Yangcheon-gu resident, Seon Min frequents this vegetable place.)

797
00:30:41,961 --> 00:30:43,061
Is it the same place?

798
00:30:44,961 --> 00:30:46,230
You should go hiking with him.

799
00:30:46,231 --> 00:30:47,960
- You should go to Mount Yongwang. - Yes.

800
00:30:47,961 --> 00:30:49,201
Mount Yongwang.

801
00:30:50,771 --> 00:30:52,870
Which refreshing fruits do you recommend?

802
00:30:52,871 --> 00:30:54,271
- These days... - I live alone.

803
00:30:54,601 --> 00:30:57,001
I'll take this. Yes, I'll take this.

804
00:30:57,101 --> 00:30:59,011
- Apples too. - Apples.

805
00:30:59,841 --> 00:31:01,110
Your total is 18 dollars.

806
00:31:01,111 --> 00:31:02,440
Did you say 18 dollars? Really?

807
00:31:02,441 --> 00:31:03,680
It's very cheap.

808
00:31:03,681 --> 00:31:05,410
(Satisfied)

809
00:31:05,411 --> 00:31:06,550
Thank you.

810
00:31:06,551 --> 00:31:09,020
- I moved to a place nearby. - I see.

811
00:31:09,021 --> 00:31:11,341
- Then you'll come often, right? - I'll try to come often.

812
00:31:12,021 --> 00:31:13,320
- Thank you. - Bye.

813
00:31:13,321 --> 00:31:14,321
Bye.

814
00:31:16,191 --> 00:31:17,661
This alley has many restaurants.

815
00:31:18,091 --> 00:31:21,761
Yangcheon-gu has so many good restaurants.

816
00:31:22,001 --> 00:31:23,201
I think you're right.

817
00:31:24,801 --> 00:31:25,971
A butchershop restaurant?

818
00:31:27,301 --> 00:31:29,377
- There are so many restaurants. - He must be hungry.

819
00:31:29,401 --> 00:31:31,040
I know. He had a long day.

820
00:31:31,041 --> 00:31:32,840
- I didn't have a single meal. - You must be very thirsty.

821
00:31:32,841 --> 00:31:34,211
I was so thirsty.

822
00:31:35,681 --> 00:31:36,981
Excuse me.

823
00:31:38,051 --> 00:31:39,210
Can I order three?

824
00:31:39,211 --> 00:31:40,650
(Unable to fight hunger, he orders food.)

825
00:31:40,651 --> 00:31:42,051
- Corndog? - I'll take six.

826
00:31:42,481 --> 00:31:43,551
Okay.

827
00:31:44,121 --> 00:31:45,190
They look tasty.

828
00:31:45,191 --> 00:31:46,420
- They're freshly-fried. - Yes.

829
00:31:46,421 --> 00:31:47,741
The freshly-fried ones are tasty.

830
00:31:48,521 --> 00:31:51,231
- I'll take 0.5L of sikhye. - Okay.

831
00:31:51,331 --> 00:31:52,861
I'll drink sikhye here.

832
00:31:54,231 --> 00:31:55,830
All right. Thank you.

833
00:31:55,831 --> 00:31:57,331
(He quickly pays.)

834
00:31:58,071 --> 00:31:59,270
(Then he downs the drink.)

835
00:31:59,271 --> 00:32:00,331
It must taste incredible.

836
00:32:01,401 --> 00:32:02,971
(Pouring in)

837
00:32:04,001 --> 00:32:05,041
Thank you.

838
00:32:06,041 --> 00:32:08,180
(Guzzling)

839
00:32:08,181 --> 00:32:09,210
He must've been thirsty.

840
00:32:09,211 --> 00:32:11,651
My goodness. You're good at drinking.

841
00:32:12,051 --> 00:32:13,411
It's bound to give him a headache.

842
00:32:14,351 --> 00:32:16,780
(Getting a headache)

843
00:32:16,781 --> 00:32:17,921
I knew it.

844
00:32:19,421 --> 00:32:21,361
They look so tasty.

845
00:32:22,021 --> 00:32:24,760
- I skipped lunch. - You must've been busy.

846
00:32:24,761 --> 00:32:26,290
- Yes, I moved today. - Did you?

847
00:32:26,291 --> 00:32:28,437
I moved to this neighborhood. I moved to Yangcheon-gu.

848
00:32:28,461 --> 00:32:30,700
- Are you a celebrity? - Yes, I'm a celebrity.

849
00:32:30,701 --> 00:32:31,801
You look familiar.

850
00:32:32,331 --> 00:32:34,171
- I'm in movies. - I was in a good mood.

851
00:32:36,301 --> 00:32:38,841
Actually, I'm an MBC announcer.

852
00:32:39,471 --> 00:32:41,080
I should've known.

853
00:32:41,081 --> 00:32:42,680
I'll come again. Thank you for the food.

854
00:32:42,681 --> 00:32:44,181
- Thank you. - Thank you.

855
00:32:45,581 --> 00:32:47,350
(He goes home with his hands heavy.)

856
00:32:47,351 --> 00:32:48,991
- The neighborhood has nice vibes. - Yes.

857
00:32:51,121 --> 00:32:52,751
(Opening)

858
00:32:53,691 --> 00:32:54,921
I hate that place.

859
00:32:56,521 --> 00:32:57,761
It stresses me out.

860
00:32:58,891 --> 00:33:00,730
I got stressed out the most in the evening.

861
00:33:00,731 --> 00:33:02,160
Anyone would get stressed out.

862
00:33:02,161 --> 00:33:04,301
- Seriously. - I feel so troubled.

863
00:33:05,301 --> 00:33:06,770
It'll take forever to put things away.

864
00:33:06,771 --> 00:33:08,671
(It's so disorganized.)

865
00:33:10,241 --> 00:33:12,071
The yellow plastic bags made it worse.

866
00:33:12,371 --> 00:33:14,011
Think of it as opening the Pokemon cards.

867
00:33:16,181 --> 00:33:17,711
How will I organize everything?

868
00:33:20,751 --> 00:33:21,920
- Hold on. - You didn't know where to start.

869
00:33:21,921 --> 00:33:24,621
That's right. I didn't know where to start.

870
00:33:25,521 --> 00:33:26,591
Firstly,

871
00:33:27,791 --> 00:33:28,921
let's take out...

872
00:33:30,091 --> 00:33:31,590
the clothes. Let's take them out...

873
00:33:31,591 --> 00:33:33,491
and put the boxes at the top.

874
00:33:34,401 --> 00:33:35,460
All right.

875
00:33:35,461 --> 00:33:37,630
Take out the items you need tomorrow.

876
00:33:37,631 --> 00:33:38,801
- Yes. - That's right.

877
00:33:41,301 --> 00:33:43,340
(He quickly hangs up clothes on hangers.)

878
00:33:43,341 --> 00:33:44,841
They're all tangled up.

879
00:33:48,011 --> 00:33:49,580
(But so many items remain.)

880
00:33:49,581 --> 00:33:50,781
Gosh, they're heavy.

881
00:33:57,451 --> 00:33:58,621
- What? - What?

882
00:34:02,121 --> 00:34:03,290
Why did the light go out?

883
00:34:03,291 --> 00:34:05,030
(Why did the bedroom suddenly turn dark?)

884
00:34:05,031 --> 00:34:06,091
It's scary.

885
00:34:07,831 --> 00:34:09,660
(It's not just the bedroom.)

886
00:34:09,661 --> 00:34:11,730
He is going to die. Something is going to jump out.

887
00:34:11,731 --> 00:34:14,471
(The entire house has been plunged into darkness.)

888
00:34:15,971 --> 00:34:17,041
What's this?

889
00:34:18,411 --> 00:34:21,411
(He comes out to the living room to figure out what's happening.)

890
00:34:22,541 --> 00:34:24,411
(Flipping the switch)

891
00:34:25,211 --> 00:34:26,981
- It must be a blackout. - So suddenly?

892
00:34:28,121 --> 00:34:29,650
(The light doesn't come back on when he flips the switch.)

893
00:34:29,651 --> 00:34:31,221
(Flustered)

894
00:34:31,821 --> 00:34:33,550
It was raining.

895
00:34:33,551 --> 00:34:34,891
- What's this? - What?

896
00:34:34,991 --> 00:34:36,711
But rain doesn't cause a blackout, does it?

897
00:34:36,761 --> 00:34:37,831
Seriously.

898
00:34:38,431 --> 00:34:40,361
- What's this? - It's scary.

899
00:34:40,461 --> 00:34:41,561
What's the matter?

900
00:34:41,831 --> 00:34:43,861
Did the breaker trip?

901
00:34:44,631 --> 00:34:45,971
Did the circus breaker trip?

902
00:34:46,331 --> 00:34:48,400
- "Circus breaker?" - Unbelievable.

903
00:34:48,401 --> 00:34:49,670
"Circus breaker?"

904
00:34:49,671 --> 00:34:50,870
Let's retake the announcer exam.

905
00:34:50,871 --> 00:34:52,711
How does one become an announcer?

906
00:34:53,141 --> 00:34:54,340
You pass the exam by being like him.

907
00:34:54,341 --> 00:34:55,511
(Joking)

908
00:34:55,681 --> 00:34:56,880
You just need to speak nonsense from time to time.

909
00:34:56,881 --> 00:34:58,080
(He was so surprised that he spoke nonsense.)

910
00:34:58,081 --> 00:34:59,911
That startled me so much. "Circus breaker."

911
00:35:01,821 --> 00:35:03,320
(He checks the message from the real estate agent...)

912
00:35:03,321 --> 00:35:05,001
(instead of going to the circuit breaker.)

913
00:35:05,251 --> 00:35:06,490
"Turning off the restroom light..."

914
00:35:06,491 --> 00:35:08,620
"flips the circuit breaker at times."

915
00:35:08,621 --> 00:35:09,820
- What? - The restroom light?

916
00:35:09,821 --> 00:35:10,960
Why does it do that?

917
00:35:10,961 --> 00:35:12,990
(Turning on the restroom light)

918
00:35:12,991 --> 00:35:14,831
Where is the circuit breaker?

919
00:35:16,801 --> 00:35:18,600
I had never experienced this on the day I moved in.

920
00:35:18,601 --> 00:35:20,671
That's right. You didn't even use electricity.

921
00:35:21,171 --> 00:35:24,871
(Is it here?)

922
00:35:25,111 --> 00:35:26,471
This is a boiler room.

923
00:35:26,671 --> 00:35:28,080
I couldn't find the circuit breaker.

924
00:35:28,081 --> 00:35:30,521
(He can't find the circuit breaker no matter where he looks.)

925
00:35:30,711 --> 00:35:32,780
- My goodness. - It's tough when that happens...

926
00:35:32,781 --> 00:35:34,750
on the day you move in.

927
00:35:34,751 --> 00:35:35,821
- I know. - Yes.

928
00:35:35,881 --> 00:35:37,180
There is so much work to be done.

929
00:35:37,181 --> 00:35:38,191
My goodness.

930
00:35:39,221 --> 00:35:40,821
I'll need to call the real estate agent.

931
00:35:42,861 --> 00:35:46,290
(He decides to get help from the real estate agent.)

932
00:35:46,291 --> 00:35:47,490
- Hello. - Hello, ma'am.

933
00:35:47,491 --> 00:35:49,500
I just moved into the house.

934
00:35:49,501 --> 00:35:50,501
Okay.

935
00:35:50,502 --> 00:35:51,730
The lights suddenly went off...

936
00:35:51,731 --> 00:35:53,571
even though the master light switch was on.

937
00:35:54,701 --> 00:35:55,871
So...

938
00:35:56,041 --> 00:35:57,671
where is the circuit breaker?

939
00:35:57,871 --> 00:36:00,110
The circuit breaker is behind...

940
00:36:00,111 --> 00:36:01,480
the master bedroom door.

941
00:36:01,481 --> 00:36:04,141
- Behind the master bedroom door? - You'll find it there. Yes.

942
00:36:04,611 --> 00:36:07,410
I see. Does it trip on its own?

943
00:36:07,411 --> 00:36:09,720
- Yes. I asked the landlord... - It suddenly tripped.

944
00:36:09,721 --> 00:36:13,091
- to get it checked. - Okay.

945
00:36:13,451 --> 00:36:16,890
- It happens sporadically. - Okay.

946
00:36:16,891 --> 00:36:19,360
- I told the landlord about it. - So that was the house you chose.

947
00:36:19,361 --> 00:36:20,430
- I see. - You chose well.

948
00:36:20,431 --> 00:36:21,731
It's a surprise.

949
00:36:22,231 --> 00:36:23,860
I got the surprise even though no one else was there.

950
00:36:23,861 --> 00:36:25,400
(There was only one at the surprise party.)

951
00:36:25,401 --> 00:36:29,340
You'll need to ask the landlord to get the electricity checked.

952
00:36:29,341 --> 00:36:31,070
Do I ask the landlord?

953
00:36:31,071 --> 00:36:33,840
- Yes, the landlord. - Okay.

954
00:36:33,841 --> 00:36:35,810
- Thank you. - Take care.

955
00:36:35,811 --> 00:36:37,357
(Planning an electricity checkup on the day of moving in?)

956
00:36:37,381 --> 00:36:38,381
(Sighing)

957
00:36:39,951 --> 00:36:41,150
(Shall I try it again?)

958
00:36:41,151 --> 00:36:42,151
(Trying to turn on the light)

959
00:36:42,152 --> 00:36:43,251
What?

960
00:36:45,151 --> 00:36:46,751
What? Why did the lights go out?

961
00:36:50,261 --> 00:36:51,361
The lights went out again.

962
00:36:52,361 --> 00:36:53,560
What's going on?

963
00:36:53,561 --> 00:36:56,631
- It isn't sporadic at all. - The meaning of "Sporadically..."

964
00:36:56,801 --> 00:36:59,001
- The electricity bill will be low. - It happens often.

965
00:37:00,131 --> 00:37:01,540
(He tries to turn the circuit breaker back on.)

966
00:37:01,541 --> 00:37:02,601
This...

967
00:37:02,941 --> 00:37:04,400
- What's going on? - Hey, what's wrong with it?

968
00:37:04,401 --> 00:37:05,441
What's going on?

969
00:37:05,811 --> 00:37:06,911
What?

970
00:37:07,571 --> 00:37:08,610
What?

971
00:37:08,611 --> 00:37:09,740
It's so scary.

972
00:37:09,741 --> 00:37:10,881
Oh, my.

973
00:37:13,681 --> 00:37:14,851
It won't explode, will it?

974
00:37:15,551 --> 00:37:17,020
Do I need to turn it on and off?

975
00:37:17,021 --> 00:37:19,290
(Do I need to turn the restroom light on and off?)

976
00:37:19,291 --> 00:37:20,820
- That place is too scary. - It's scary.

977
00:37:20,821 --> 00:37:21,981
I can't live in such a place.

978
00:37:23,121 --> 00:37:25,721
(He turns on the circuit breaker while the restroom light is on.)

979
00:37:25,961 --> 00:37:27,130
Why does it do that?

980
00:37:27,131 --> 00:37:28,331
(The lights turn back on.)

981
00:37:29,001 --> 00:37:32,171
(Even though the lights are on...)

982
00:37:32,831 --> 00:37:33,970
(Why did this happen?)

983
00:37:33,971 --> 00:37:35,801
You need to figure out what the matter is.

984
00:37:36,441 --> 00:37:38,870
When I turn off the restroom light, the circuit breaker trips.

985
00:37:38,871 --> 00:37:39,941
- What? - What?

986
00:37:40,071 --> 00:37:41,871
Once you turn it off, there is no going back.

987
00:37:41,981 --> 00:37:44,440
The wires must be fused...

988
00:37:44,441 --> 00:37:46,351
- with the restroom light switch. - I guess so.

989
00:37:46,951 --> 00:37:48,271
Yangcheon-gu isn't an easy place.

990
00:37:48,951 --> 00:37:50,281
People welcomed me, but...

991
00:37:50,681 --> 00:37:52,950
- There is a hazing ritual. - Yes.

992
00:37:52,951 --> 00:37:55,121
But the landlord fixed it today.

993
00:37:55,421 --> 00:37:56,661
- It got fixed. - I see.

994
00:37:57,761 --> 00:38:00,191
It happens. Yes.

995
00:38:00,791 --> 00:38:03,031
I'm hungry. I'll need to eat dinner first.

996
00:38:03,531 --> 00:38:06,201
Which menu yields the least amount of trash?

997
00:38:08,071 --> 00:38:09,170
Jjajangmyeon.

998
00:38:09,171 --> 00:38:11,141
You should eat jjajangmyeon on the moving day.

999
00:38:11,971 --> 00:38:15,440
(He looks up nearby Chinese restaurants.)

1000
00:38:15,441 --> 00:38:17,951
The minimum order is 19 dollars. It's too expensive.

1001
00:38:18,551 --> 00:38:20,881
I can't order 19 dollars' worth of food by myself.

1002
00:38:21,251 --> 00:38:22,780
- It's too expensive. - The expenses will rise...

1003
00:38:22,781 --> 00:38:23,950
to 1,100 dollars.

1004
00:38:23,951 --> 00:38:25,497
(It'll happen if you try to meet the minimum order.)

1005
00:38:25,521 --> 00:38:26,750
The minimum order is 15 dollars.

1006
00:38:26,751 --> 00:38:28,091
Fifteen dollars isn't so bad.

1007
00:38:29,121 --> 00:38:31,161
Double portion of jjajangmyeon...

1008
00:38:33,031 --> 00:38:34,491
and fried dumplings.

1009
00:38:35,261 --> 00:38:37,930
Because of the minimum order,

1010
00:38:37,931 --> 00:38:40,900
I haven't ordered jjajangmyeon in a long while.

1011
00:38:40,901 --> 00:38:42,381
Right. Unless there are two people...

1012
00:38:43,201 --> 00:38:45,270
Let's put them on the bed.

1013
00:38:45,271 --> 00:38:46,887
(Let's resume unpacking before the food arrives.)

1014
00:38:46,911 --> 00:38:48,881
(He picks up the bag with clothes inside.)

1015
00:38:50,141 --> 00:38:51,141
(He empties it on the bed.)

1016
00:38:51,142 --> 00:38:53,310
Socks on the bed?

1017
00:38:53,311 --> 00:38:54,821
(He empties it on the bed.)

1018
00:38:55,421 --> 00:38:58,790
(He tosses the empty bag in front of him.)

1019
00:38:58,791 --> 00:39:00,421
I just need a place to sleep.

1020
00:39:01,461 --> 00:39:03,260
(I need a place to eat dinner.)

1021
00:39:03,261 --> 00:39:05,361
I have so much stuff.

1022
00:39:06,331 --> 00:39:08,201
(Heave-ho)

1023
00:39:09,131 --> 00:39:10,231
Throw away the whole thing.

1024
00:39:12,901 --> 00:39:14,370
Seriously, what should I do?

1025
00:39:14,371 --> 00:39:16,571
(He can't throw them out so he puts them on the floor.)

1026
00:39:16,671 --> 00:39:19,871
(I need eating utensils to have dinner.)

1027
00:39:20,611 --> 00:39:22,641
(Heavy)

1028
00:39:23,811 --> 00:39:26,611
(Grimacing, he picks up tableware.)

1029
00:39:30,251 --> 00:39:32,551
(It falls to the floor.)

1030
00:39:34,621 --> 00:39:37,361
It's hardy. It didn't break. This whiskey glass is...

1031
00:39:38,161 --> 00:39:39,230
definitely hardy.

1032
00:39:39,231 --> 00:39:41,261
(He overcomes most things with optimism.)

1033
00:39:41,461 --> 00:39:44,061
Had it broken, it would've been bad energy.

1034
00:39:44,201 --> 00:39:46,100
It didn't break, so it was good energy.

1035
00:39:46,101 --> 00:39:47,201
- Right. - It didn't break.

1036
00:39:48,841 --> 00:39:50,170
I'll put them in the overhead cabinet.

1037
00:39:50,171 --> 00:39:51,871
(Opening)

1038
00:39:52,111 --> 00:39:53,211
(Slamming shut)

1039
00:39:54,711 --> 00:39:55,841
What is it this time?

1040
00:39:58,011 --> 00:39:59,581
Why does it close on its own?

1041
00:40:00,111 --> 00:40:01,281
It doesn't stay open.

1042
00:40:04,851 --> 00:40:06,421
You didn't check a single thing.

1043
00:40:06,791 --> 00:40:08,351
He just went, "How nice," and moved in.

1044
00:40:09,061 --> 00:40:10,120
It's not like that.

1045
00:40:10,121 --> 00:40:11,931
"There is an elevator? How nice."

1046
00:40:12,661 --> 00:40:14,060
Landlords love such tenants.

1047
00:40:14,061 --> 00:40:15,161
(Embarrassed)

1048
00:40:15,731 --> 00:40:17,530
(Kang Yong, let's use your head.)

1049
00:40:17,531 --> 00:40:18,531
(Supporting)

1050
00:40:18,532 --> 00:40:19,931
- That's right. - There you go.

1051
00:40:20,571 --> 00:40:21,770
This place is fun.

1052
00:40:21,771 --> 00:40:23,291
(He supports the door with his brain.)

1053
00:40:23,871 --> 00:40:25,871
(I'm not sure about this.)

1054
00:40:26,711 --> 00:40:28,591
The cabinet door closed as soon as I opened it.

1055
00:40:29,241 --> 00:40:30,941
I definitely checked it before moving in.

1056
00:40:32,151 --> 00:40:34,111
But it seems like I should've been more thorough.

1057
00:40:34,581 --> 00:40:36,281
Since I checked out many places...

1058
00:40:36,451 --> 00:40:37,480
The last tenant left this here.

1059
00:40:37,481 --> 00:40:39,851
I only checked if the major components were okay...

1060
00:40:40,021 --> 00:40:41,497
- and didn't go further. - There are so many.

1061
00:40:41,521 --> 00:40:43,360
I only checked the big components, so I missed the cabinet door.

1062
00:40:43,361 --> 00:40:44,761
(It was my bad.)

1063
00:40:46,031 --> 00:40:48,030
(He takes note of the cabinet door and resumes unpacking.)

1064
00:40:48,031 --> 00:40:49,601
- Yes? - It's a delivery.

1065
00:40:52,871 --> 00:40:54,670
Thank you.

1066
00:40:54,671 --> 00:40:56,041
(Jjajangmyeon arrives.)

1067
00:40:58,341 --> 00:41:00,671
(Inching over)

1068
00:41:01,711 --> 00:41:06,680
(Kang Yong always ate at a floor table in the past.)

1069
00:41:06,681 --> 00:41:09,551
(From today onward, he'll eat at a proper table.)

1070
00:41:11,591 --> 00:41:13,351
Where are the chopsticks?

1071
00:41:13,651 --> 00:41:15,491
(Rummaging)

1072
00:41:17,821 --> 00:41:20,391
(He takes chopsticks out of the ziplock bag...)

1073
00:41:22,861 --> 00:41:25,070
(and rinses the tip with water.)

1074
00:41:25,071 --> 00:41:26,171
Let's eat first.

1075
00:41:27,631 --> 00:41:28,801
He should eat on the floor.

1076
00:41:29,001 --> 00:41:30,171
There is no floor.

1077
00:41:31,071 --> 00:41:32,071
Look at that.

1078
00:41:32,072 --> 00:41:33,941
(Climbing)

1079
00:41:34,741 --> 00:41:38,281
(He steps on the luggage to go to the table.)

1080
00:41:38,651 --> 00:41:39,651
(Groaning)

1081
00:41:40,411 --> 00:41:42,621
Gosh, this is ridiculous. This is nonsense.

1082
00:41:48,191 --> 00:41:49,521
The house is too cramped.

1083
00:41:50,191 --> 00:41:51,991
He looks rich because there is so much stuff.

1084
00:41:54,391 --> 00:41:55,460
Let's eat first.

1085
00:41:55,461 --> 00:41:57,731
(Let's eat first.)

1086
00:41:58,631 --> 00:42:00,731
The dumplings are hot. I love it.

1087
00:42:01,741 --> 00:42:03,200
- They look tasty. - They look nice.

1088
00:42:03,201 --> 00:42:04,671
(He takes a bite of a dumpling.)

1089
00:42:08,711 --> 00:42:09,740
(Gosh, it's hot.)

1090
00:42:09,741 --> 00:42:10,941
Gosh, I'm hungry.

1091
00:42:12,181 --> 00:42:15,381
(Although it's hot, he is thankful that he can eat.)

1092
00:42:16,981 --> 00:42:18,290
(He hurriedly mixes the jjajangmyeon.)

1093
00:42:18,291 --> 00:42:20,767
- The noodles aren't soggy at all. - The restaurant must be close.

1094
00:42:20,791 --> 00:42:24,491
Jjajangmyeon should be eaten amidst the unpacked luggage.

1095
00:42:24,761 --> 00:42:27,631
- You eat like that when you move. - That's right.

1096
00:42:28,161 --> 00:42:30,000
- That's the moving day swagger. - That's right.

1097
00:42:30,001 --> 00:42:31,200
You eat on the floor with the newspaper spread out.

1098
00:42:31,201 --> 00:42:32,970
You can only do that on the moving day.

1099
00:42:32,971 --> 00:42:34,731
(His first meal has the moving day swagger.)

1100
00:42:35,701 --> 00:42:38,271
(Slurping)

1101
00:42:42,181 --> 00:42:43,910
(Impressed)

1102
00:42:43,911 --> 00:42:45,231
This restaurant makes tasty food.

1103
00:42:45,681 --> 00:42:46,780
(He puts his foot on the luggage in a cool way.)

1104
00:42:46,781 --> 00:42:47,881
Swagger.

1105
00:42:48,121 --> 00:42:49,851
I had nowhere to put my foot.

1106
00:42:50,851 --> 00:42:53,291
(Inhaling food)

1107
00:42:53,791 --> 00:42:56,620
(Slurping)

1108
00:42:56,621 --> 00:42:58,490
- The first meal must've been tasty. - Of course.

1109
00:42:58,491 --> 00:42:59,631
(Salivating)

1110
00:43:01,391 --> 00:43:03,861
(Swinging his hand)

1111
00:43:04,231 --> 00:43:05,970
(Looking around)

1112
00:43:05,971 --> 00:43:07,071
There is no napkin.

1113
00:43:07,401 --> 00:43:08,501
Use your clothes.

1114
00:43:09,901 --> 00:43:11,571
It's in there somewhere.

1115
00:43:12,771 --> 00:43:14,641
(Grabbing)

1116
00:43:14,841 --> 00:43:16,617
(He takes off the plastic wrap from the fried dumplings.)

1117
00:43:16,641 --> 00:43:17,881
There you go.

1118
00:43:20,581 --> 00:43:22,081
No way.

1119
00:43:25,591 --> 00:43:29,091
(For goodness' sake)

1120
00:43:29,791 --> 00:43:31,460
She said it was sporadic.

1121
00:43:31,461 --> 00:43:34,091
I think you need to burn that gratitude journal.

1122
00:43:34,901 --> 00:43:35,961
That's right.

1123
00:43:36,061 --> 00:43:37,801
(Sighing)

1124
00:43:38,501 --> 00:43:41,101
(He turns on the cellphone flashlight.)

1125
00:43:42,071 --> 00:43:44,301
- Oh, no. - I was too hungry.

1126
00:43:46,711 --> 00:43:47,870
How cozy.

1127
00:43:47,871 --> 00:43:49,181
(Slurping)

1128
00:43:52,881 --> 00:43:55,281
(Slurping)

1129
00:43:58,081 --> 00:44:01,221
(He eats a piece of pickled radish as well.)

1130
00:44:01,351 --> 00:44:03,121
You know, the lights...

1131
00:44:05,891 --> 00:44:06,991
What an event.

1132
00:44:07,231 --> 00:44:09,000
- The pattern is unpredictable. - I know.

1133
00:44:09,001 --> 00:44:10,401
(Getting up)

1134
00:44:11,001 --> 00:44:12,470
I have no strength to jump down.

1135
00:44:12,471 --> 00:44:13,900
(He navigates his way to turn on the lights.)

1136
00:44:13,901 --> 00:44:15,371
It's as if the house is alive.

1137
00:44:16,571 --> 00:44:17,931
The monthly rent is 1,050 dollars.

1138
00:44:18,311 --> 00:44:19,970
Who turns on a flashlight inside the house?

1139
00:44:19,971 --> 00:44:22,171
- For goodness' sake. - It lowers the electricity bill.

1140
00:44:24,111 --> 00:44:25,310
(It's his 3rd time looking for a circuit breaker in the dark.)

1141
00:44:25,311 --> 00:44:26,410
This is a serious problem.

1142
00:44:26,411 --> 00:44:28,891
(It's his 3rd time looking for a circuit breaker in the dark.)

1143
00:44:31,121 --> 00:44:32,191
Good.

1144
00:44:33,121 --> 00:44:35,991
(The house lights up again.)

1145
00:44:36,391 --> 00:44:37,891
Let's eat first.

1146
00:44:39,991 --> 00:44:42,061
I'd be too scared to live in a house like that.

1147
00:44:42,731 --> 00:44:45,571
- Kian84 would've gone to a motel. - I can't live in a house like that.

1148
00:44:45,671 --> 00:44:47,101
I find it too scary.

1149
00:44:48,971 --> 00:44:50,201
It's okay. This is...

1150
00:44:51,711 --> 00:44:52,971
how you learn.

1151
00:44:53,341 --> 00:44:54,371
Learn what?

1152
00:44:55,711 --> 00:44:56,780
Learn what?

1153
00:44:56,781 --> 00:44:59,451
(Learn what?)

1154
00:44:59,951 --> 00:45:01,381
You sounded like a grandpa.

1155
00:45:01,621 --> 00:45:02,780
- "Learn what?" - "Learn what?"

1156
00:45:02,781 --> 00:45:03,821
Learn what?

1157
00:45:04,751 --> 00:45:05,951
Just what do you learn?

1158
00:45:07,651 --> 00:45:09,421
(This grandpa is curious.)

1159
00:45:09,591 --> 00:45:11,391
When I viewed the house,

1160
00:45:12,291 --> 00:45:14,231
I had no idea that the lights went out often.

1161
00:45:15,131 --> 00:45:16,731
Right? There was no way of knowing that.

1162
00:45:16,931 --> 00:45:19,331
- You'll check next time. - Yes, I'll do that next time.

1163
00:45:20,231 --> 00:45:21,300
(He inhales the food hurriedly before the lights go out again.)

1164
00:45:21,301 --> 00:45:23,661
I wanted to finish eating before the lights went out again.

1165
00:45:23,871 --> 00:45:25,141
- Right. - It looks tasty.

1166
00:45:27,311 --> 00:45:28,481
I'm full.

1167
00:45:34,151 --> 00:45:35,421
I almost got an upset stomach.

1168
00:45:36,081 --> 00:45:37,350
There is so much work to be done.

1169
00:45:37,351 --> 00:45:39,427
(There is a mountain of bags that need to be unpacked.)

1170
00:45:39,451 --> 00:45:40,931
I don't think I'll be finished today.

1171
00:45:41,291 --> 00:45:42,421
This is bad.

1172
00:45:43,261 --> 00:45:46,561
(Dazed)

1173
00:45:48,301 --> 00:45:50,701
(Getting up)

1174
00:45:55,271 --> 00:45:58,841
(I must still do it.)

1175
00:46:01,541 --> 00:46:03,211
(Standing up)

1176
00:46:03,781 --> 00:46:06,581
I felt joy, sorrow, and happiness today.

1177
00:46:07,111 --> 00:46:09,620
I felt so happy in the morning when I packed my things.

1178
00:46:09,621 --> 00:46:11,251
I felt a sense of relief...

1179
00:46:11,351 --> 00:46:13,291
at the fact that I was moving to a bigger place.

1180
00:46:14,151 --> 00:46:16,191
I felt happy and wanted to leave quickly.

1181
00:46:16,421 --> 00:46:19,290
I felt frustrated when I arrived and brought up my things.

1182
00:46:19,291 --> 00:46:21,491
I missed my parents as well.

1183
00:46:22,001 --> 00:46:23,331
That was when I felt sorrow.

1184
00:46:23,361 --> 00:46:24,961
But even after that,

1185
00:46:25,201 --> 00:46:27,570
I imagined myself having a living room...

1186
00:46:27,571 --> 00:46:29,241
after sleeping in my room.

1187
00:46:29,901 --> 00:46:31,771
That filled me up with happiness.

1188
00:46:32,111 --> 00:46:34,210
There was only an entrance in a studio apartment.

1189
00:46:34,211 --> 00:46:36,711
But there will be a living room in a one-bedroom apartment.

1190
00:46:37,041 --> 00:46:38,550
I felt a lot of excitement for that.

1191
00:46:38,551 --> 00:46:40,451
- You'll be getting an extra room. - Right.

1192
00:46:41,081 --> 00:46:42,081
I'll try to get it done as soon as I can...

1193
00:46:42,081 --> 00:46:43,081
without overdoing it...

1194
00:46:43,082 --> 00:46:45,191
to get my things sorted.

1195
00:46:45,551 --> 00:46:46,591
After getting off work,

1196
00:46:47,221 --> 00:46:49,761
I will sort two bags a day.

1197
00:46:50,921 --> 00:46:53,631
Won't that take 1 or 2 weeks if I sort 2 bags a day?

1198
00:46:54,261 --> 00:46:56,501
I'll try to do that. Two bags a day.

1199
00:47:01,101 --> 00:47:02,470
I should hang it up there later.

1200
00:47:02,471 --> 00:47:04,271
The lucky broom my mom gave me.

1201
00:47:06,511 --> 00:47:08,110
It should go up there after bringing that down.

1202
00:47:08,111 --> 00:47:09,911
- Right. - Right.

1203
00:47:11,711 --> 00:47:13,011
How's the house right now?

1204
00:47:13,411 --> 00:47:15,351
Everything is sorted now.

1205
00:47:15,551 --> 00:47:17,180
- It took me a week. - Did you get things thrown out?

1206
00:47:17,181 --> 00:47:20,050
I got rid of a third of what I had.

1207
00:47:20,051 --> 00:47:22,220
I have a lot less now.

1208
00:47:22,221 --> 00:47:24,101
(It's neat now after sorting out 2 bags a day.)

1209
00:47:24,161 --> 00:47:27,031
(The bedroom that had no space...)

1210
00:47:27,791 --> 00:47:30,531
(looks quite cozy now.)

1211
00:47:31,461 --> 00:47:34,170
The repairman came today to fix the circuit breaker.

1212
00:47:34,171 --> 00:47:35,470
- Really? - That's a relief.

1213
00:47:35,471 --> 00:47:38,671
When you empty the house first, it can get filled with other things.

1214
00:47:38,811 --> 00:47:41,470
When you continue to grow and live in a bigger place,

1215
00:47:41,471 --> 00:47:43,181
- it will be great. - Right.

1216
00:47:43,211 --> 00:47:44,211
Congratulations!

1217
00:47:44,212 --> 00:47:47,280
(Congratulations on moving.)

1218
00:47:47,281 --> 00:47:48,281
(I Live Alone)

1219
00:47:49,051 --> 00:47:50,150
(Fathermoo)

1220
00:47:50,151 --> 00:47:51,991
- "Fathermoo." - "Fathermoo."

1221
00:47:53,991 --> 00:47:57,121
(Hyun Moo is fast asleep.)

1222
00:48:06,231 --> 00:48:07,300
(Groaning)

1223
00:48:07,301 --> 00:48:08,601
Gosh.

1224
00:48:09,501 --> 00:48:10,940
Gosh, Hyun Moo!

1225
00:48:10,941 --> 00:48:11,941
(Worried)

1226
00:48:13,241 --> 00:48:15,811
(He turns off the alarm while groaning.)

1227
00:48:17,141 --> 00:48:18,180
(Current time: 7am)

1228
00:48:18,181 --> 00:48:20,380
He got up so early. He wakes up so early now.

1229
00:48:20,381 --> 00:48:21,411
Get some more sleep!

1230
00:48:23,581 --> 00:48:27,891
(He wakes up with his eyes half-open.)

1231
00:48:28,821 --> 00:48:30,761
(Looking around)

1232
00:48:32,161 --> 00:48:33,830
Why does it feel like a long-term care hospital?

1233
00:48:33,831 --> 00:48:35,030
- Gosh. - Gosh.

1234
00:48:35,031 --> 00:48:36,951
Gosh, what's the point of living in a big house?

1235
00:48:39,101 --> 00:48:40,471
I feel pitiful, don't I?

1236
00:48:40,671 --> 00:48:42,770
- Oh, gosh! - I look like an old man, don't I?

1237
00:48:42,771 --> 00:48:44,140
- No. - It's not that bad?

1238
00:48:44,141 --> 00:48:45,347
- It's not that bad. - You'll recover.

1239
00:48:45,371 --> 00:48:46,441
I will?

1240
00:48:48,441 --> 00:48:50,411
(Grabbing)

1241
00:48:51,241 --> 00:48:52,980
(Opening wide)

1242
00:48:52,981 --> 00:48:54,751
Why did he wake up so early?

1243
00:48:56,281 --> 00:48:59,851
(He heads to the living room after picking something up.)

1244
00:49:01,151 --> 00:49:03,261
What? Why is it like this?

1245
00:49:03,521 --> 00:49:04,761
- What? - What?

1246
00:49:06,861 --> 00:49:10,600
(The living room is a mess?)

1247
00:49:10,601 --> 00:49:12,501
What's going on? Why is it like that?

1248
00:49:14,171 --> 00:49:15,500
(A shoe is lying around on the floor.)

1249
00:49:15,501 --> 00:49:18,240
- Why is one shoe there? - Look at that.

1250
00:49:18,241 --> 00:49:20,110
- I got so surprised. - Gosh!

1251
00:49:20,111 --> 00:49:21,211
Was that on top?

1252
00:49:22,011 --> 00:49:23,910
- It was robbed. - Gosh!

1253
00:49:23,911 --> 00:49:25,011
Oh, no.

1254
00:49:27,411 --> 00:49:30,221
You little punk!

1255
00:49:31,621 --> 00:49:32,621
What?

1256
00:49:32,622 --> 00:49:34,820
- You little punk! - It's a dog! Gosh!

1257
00:49:34,821 --> 00:49:36,661
- It's so cute! - It's so cute!

1258
00:49:37,561 --> 00:49:38,760
(I got the intruder.)

1259
00:49:38,761 --> 00:49:40,991
- How cute! - You little punk!

1260
00:49:41,231 --> 00:49:42,401
You little punk!

1261
00:49:43,331 --> 00:49:45,201
It's the project you've all been waiting for.

1262
00:49:45,331 --> 00:49:49,101
It's Part 2 of Jun Hyun Moo's 5-year good son project.

1263
00:49:50,101 --> 00:49:53,141
Part One was to find a place in Gimpo.

1264
00:49:54,011 --> 00:49:56,511
It was the project to live in a place near my parents.

1265
00:49:58,041 --> 00:49:59,980
(No. That can't happen!)

1266
00:49:59,981 --> 00:50:01,280
It was a failure.

1267
00:50:01,281 --> 00:50:02,951
(Failed)

1268
00:50:03,151 --> 00:50:04,250
Part Two...

1269
00:50:04,251 --> 00:50:06,690
- is this fellow. - It's so cute.

1270
00:50:06,691 --> 00:50:08,691
- It's a very gentle dog. - It's so small.

1271
00:50:09,761 --> 00:50:13,931
It's the dog my mother and father raise.

1272
00:50:14,391 --> 00:50:16,000
It's a mix between...

1273
00:50:16,001 --> 00:50:17,601
a Coton de Tulear and a Bichon Frise.

1274
00:50:18,301 --> 00:50:19,471
How old is it?

1275
00:50:19,771 --> 00:50:20,801
It's 70 days old.

1276
00:50:21,031 --> 00:50:22,111
- What? - It's 70 days old.

1277
00:50:22,741 --> 00:50:26,011
It was rescued from a puppy mill.

1278
00:50:26,371 --> 00:50:28,641
It's very mild and obedient.

1279
00:50:29,341 --> 00:50:31,780
- Kian84 made an adoption recently. - Right.

1280
00:50:31,781 --> 00:50:34,281
I asked him to introduce the person in charge to me.

1281
00:50:36,051 --> 00:50:37,980
Abandoned dog adoption and running.

1282
00:50:37,981 --> 00:50:39,691
(He even adopted an abandoned dog.)

1283
00:50:39,821 --> 00:50:42,860
You won't leave even a bit of space when you follow him.

1284
00:50:42,861 --> 00:50:45,121
- I copy it right away. - You copy it right away.

1285
00:50:45,261 --> 00:50:46,560
I'll meet Ito Junji next week.

1286
00:50:46,561 --> 00:50:49,361
(I'll meet Ito Junji next week.)

1287
00:50:50,261 --> 00:50:52,200
- Ito Junji. - I'm in trouble.

1288
00:50:52,201 --> 00:50:53,881
(Painting, running, dog, and Mooto Junji?)

1289
00:50:54,271 --> 00:50:57,501
I should've gotten married and brought them a grandchild.

1290
00:50:57,901 --> 00:51:00,340
This fellow is playing the role of a grandchild.

1291
00:51:00,341 --> 00:51:02,241
The two feel a lot of joy thanks to this dog.

1292
00:51:02,541 --> 00:51:06,550
It's hard for my parents to take care of things like...

1293
00:51:06,551 --> 00:51:07,950
the vaccination dates.

1294
00:51:07,951 --> 00:51:09,781
It's hard for them to reach the vet as well.

1295
00:51:09,921 --> 00:51:12,951
The dog was sent to me from my parents.

1296
00:51:13,191 --> 00:51:15,220
So you can take care of those things for them?

1297
00:51:15,221 --> 00:51:16,867
(He will be a good son by taking care of the dog for a day.)

1298
00:51:16,891 --> 00:51:19,261
You little punk!

1299
00:51:19,361 --> 00:51:21,061
Gosh! It's a helicopter!

1300
00:51:22,931 --> 00:51:24,001
Gosh!

1301
00:51:27,431 --> 00:51:29,501
Its fur is so cute. The grubby fur.

1302
00:51:29,641 --> 00:51:30,941
Was that so?

1303
00:51:31,041 --> 00:51:32,070
- It smells so pleasant. - Oh, right.

1304
00:51:32,071 --> 00:51:33,970
It's like that for all puppies.

1305
00:51:33,971 --> 00:51:36,341
- Is that so? - They can't get groomed now.

1306
00:51:36,581 --> 00:51:37,981
They must be over six months old.

1307
00:51:38,341 --> 00:51:41,411
They all look grubby before that.

1308
00:51:41,481 --> 00:51:43,420
- The expert. - Right. She's the dog expert.

1309
00:51:43,421 --> 00:51:45,591
Right. The dog grooming expert.

1310
00:51:46,621 --> 00:51:49,391
(He gets up after rubbing its grubby fur.)

1311
00:51:51,791 --> 00:51:54,531
(Yawning)

1312
00:51:57,001 --> 00:51:58,031
You punk!

1313
00:51:59,131 --> 00:52:00,400
(Watching)

1314
00:52:00,401 --> 00:52:02,701
- Gosh! - It's so cute!

1315
00:52:03,241 --> 00:52:04,270
It's so cute.

1316
00:52:04,271 --> 00:52:06,270
- Why are dogs so cute? - Gosh. Look at it...

1317
00:52:06,271 --> 00:52:07,951
- staying so focused already. - Let's see.

1318
00:52:08,171 --> 00:52:09,580
(Following)

1319
00:52:09,581 --> 00:52:10,581
Let's see.

1320
00:52:11,181 --> 00:52:12,711
Did you make a mess?

1321
00:52:14,151 --> 00:52:15,151
What?

1322
00:52:15,581 --> 00:52:17,521
- Where? No way! - Did it make a mess?

1323
00:52:19,599 --> 00:52:20,629
What?

1324
00:52:22,569 --> 00:52:24,039
Why did you bring my shoe here?

1325
00:52:24,369 --> 00:52:25,439
You pooped...

1326
00:52:27,969 --> 00:52:30,179
I think it pooped there thinking that was the dog pad.

1327
00:52:31,209 --> 00:52:33,409
You little punk! I thought you were doing well.

1328
00:52:34,709 --> 00:52:36,179
Good job.

1329
00:52:36,579 --> 00:52:37,579
"Good job?"

1330
00:52:40,489 --> 00:52:42,489
This never happened. Why did it poop here?

1331
00:52:43,259 --> 00:52:45,089
You peed here well.

1332
00:52:46,289 --> 00:52:49,029
Why did it poop here?

1333
00:52:50,499 --> 00:52:52,699
It happened last night seeing how hard it is.

1334
00:52:53,629 --> 00:52:56,099
Did you make a mistake or not?

1335
00:52:57,539 --> 00:52:58,539
You little punk!

1336
00:52:58,540 --> 00:52:59,569
(Feeling bad)

1337
00:53:00,139 --> 00:53:03,009
(He heads to the bathroom to take care of the mess.)

1338
00:53:03,909 --> 00:53:05,848
It's a big relief that it wasn't pee.

1339
00:53:05,849 --> 00:53:07,849
- No way. Again? - There it goes.

1340
00:53:07,909 --> 00:53:08,948
It's pee this time.

1341
00:53:08,949 --> 00:53:11,588
(Peeing)

1342
00:53:11,589 --> 00:53:13,989
- I didn't know. - Pee is more troublesome.

1343
00:53:16,489 --> 00:53:17,958
The color of the carpet makes it harder to tell.

1344
00:53:17,959 --> 00:53:19,358
What happened?

1345
00:53:19,359 --> 00:53:21,558
- That would be hard to tell. - That would be hard to tell.

1346
00:53:21,559 --> 00:53:22,598
I didn't know.

1347
00:53:22,599 --> 00:53:23,679
(He doesn't know anything.)

1348
00:53:24,259 --> 00:53:26,699
(He picks up the shoe without noticing about the pee.)

1349
00:53:27,299 --> 00:53:28,839
How did it bring this heavy shoe?

1350
00:53:29,069 --> 00:53:31,198
- I wonder. - The dog must have...

1351
00:53:31,199 --> 00:53:32,809
- pretty strong teeth. - Right.

1352
00:53:34,039 --> 00:53:35,308
(Following)

1353
00:53:35,309 --> 00:53:36,709
It's following Hyun Moo everywhere.

1354
00:53:38,449 --> 00:53:39,849
Gosh, this is fascinating.

1355
00:53:40,409 --> 00:53:41,509
No.

1356
00:53:41,819 --> 00:53:43,218
No. Leave it here.

1357
00:53:43,219 --> 00:53:45,495
(The dog followed Hyun Moo all the way to the shoe closet.)

1358
00:53:45,519 --> 00:53:46,919
I should give the dog some water.

1359
00:53:50,219 --> 00:53:51,519
I'll give you more water.

1360
00:53:52,589 --> 00:53:54,258
The eyes, nose, and mouth are close to each other.

1361
00:53:54,259 --> 00:53:55,998
(Is that so?)

1362
00:53:55,999 --> 00:53:57,929
- Right. - The dog looks like Dong Yeob.

1363
00:53:59,269 --> 00:54:02,069
- It's so cute. - That makes it cuter.

1364
00:54:02,839 --> 00:54:05,869
(Pouring)

1365
00:54:07,169 --> 00:54:09,638
(A refill of clean water)

1366
00:54:09,639 --> 00:54:10,739
Water?

1367
00:54:11,849 --> 00:54:13,478
(Here's some water.)

1368
00:54:13,479 --> 00:54:15,348
Here. Have some water.

1369
00:54:15,349 --> 00:54:16,679
(Slurping)

1370
00:54:17,549 --> 00:54:20,749
(He prepares the dog food as well.)

1371
00:54:21,119 --> 00:54:22,989
(Peeking)

1372
00:54:23,589 --> 00:54:25,359
It was put in Dad's medicine bag.

1373
00:54:26,259 --> 00:54:28,729
A bit of milk powder was sprinkled on top.

1374
00:54:31,559 --> 00:54:34,969
(The dog food with milk powder gets carefully handed.)

1375
00:54:36,969 --> 00:54:38,669
Here. Take a look at this.

1376
00:54:42,839 --> 00:54:44,838
- Here's your food. - Why won't it eat?

1377
00:54:44,839 --> 00:54:46,709
(Sniffing)

1378
00:54:48,009 --> 00:54:49,219
Why won't it eat?

1379
00:54:49,379 --> 00:54:51,549
Puppies usually go wild when they see food.

1380
00:54:52,149 --> 00:54:53,348
Your food is on the plate.

1381
00:54:53,349 --> 00:54:54,389
(Squirming)

1382
00:54:55,889 --> 00:54:56,889
(Sitting)

1383
00:54:56,890 --> 00:54:58,610
Gosh! The dog placed its bottom on his lap!

1384
00:54:59,289 --> 00:55:00,728
That's so cute.

1385
00:55:00,729 --> 00:55:03,229
(A dad's smile)

1386
00:55:05,199 --> 00:55:06,998
What? Did it start to eat when the food was in your hand?

1387
00:55:06,999 --> 00:55:08,069
Right.

1388
00:55:09,039 --> 00:55:10,968
Right. Go ahead and eat.

1389
00:55:10,969 --> 00:55:15,239
(It starts to eat after taking a bite from his hand.)

1390
00:55:17,539 --> 00:55:19,049
Gosh, it's all because of you.

1391
00:55:20,109 --> 00:55:22,179
I was supposed to sleep in.

1392
00:55:22,679 --> 00:55:24,479
Did you wake up early to feed the dog?

1393
00:55:24,679 --> 00:55:25,718
There were set times...

1394
00:55:25,719 --> 00:55:27,189
- of when the dog was fed. - Right.

1395
00:55:28,489 --> 00:55:31,359
(Fathermoo feeds the dog after giving up on his sleep.)

1396
00:55:32,759 --> 00:55:34,458
- It's very gentle. - It's a quiet dog.

1397
00:55:34,459 --> 00:55:35,799
- It won't bark at all. - Right.

1398
00:55:37,329 --> 00:55:38,428
It's a nice dog.

1399
00:55:38,429 --> 00:55:39,798
(It's a nice dog.)

1400
00:55:39,799 --> 00:55:40,899
I feel so proud.

1401
00:55:42,699 --> 00:55:44,538
(Fathermoo feels proud to see the dog eats well.)

1402
00:55:44,539 --> 00:55:45,909
You're done!

1403
00:55:46,739 --> 00:55:48,068
- You're done! - Gosh.

1404
00:55:48,069 --> 00:55:49,139
How cute.

1405
00:55:49,739 --> 00:55:51,909
The dog must be fed at the right times.

1406
00:55:53,149 --> 00:55:55,478
You're done now.

1407
00:55:55,479 --> 00:55:57,179
(That was great.)

1408
00:55:58,919 --> 00:56:00,649
What should you be called?

1409
00:56:01,089 --> 00:56:02,259
Come here.

1410
00:56:02,659 --> 00:56:04,059
So the dog doesn't have a name yet.

1411
00:56:06,559 --> 00:56:08,089
Sunmoo? Are you Sunmoo?

1412
00:56:08,929 --> 00:56:09,999
Sunmoo?

1413
00:56:11,199 --> 00:56:12,869
Baekseolgi? Injeolmi?

1414
00:56:13,729 --> 00:56:15,099
It's such a cute dog.

1415
00:56:15,869 --> 00:56:17,469
(Thinking)

1416
00:56:18,099 --> 00:56:20,409
(Getting up)

1417
00:56:25,649 --> 00:56:29,249
(Moomoo calls someone.)

1418
00:56:35,319 --> 00:56:36,358
- Hello? - Hey, Dad.

1419
00:56:36,359 --> 00:56:37,559
Are you going to the hospital?

1420
00:56:37,759 --> 00:56:38,889
I won't go today.

1421
00:56:38,959 --> 00:56:40,799
It's my first time hearing his father's voice.

1422
00:56:40,859 --> 00:56:42,199
When will you be going then?

1423
00:56:42,299 --> 00:56:43,798
They will perform scans every three months...

1424
00:56:43,799 --> 00:56:46,599
to look for anything bad.

1425
00:56:47,769 --> 00:56:48,769
- Gosh! - Gosh!

1426
00:56:48,770 --> 00:56:49,899
It's so cute.

1427
00:56:50,269 --> 00:56:52,439
- Things are looking good for now? - Right.

1428
00:56:52,839 --> 00:56:54,338
He called himself a bad son,

1429
00:56:54,339 --> 00:56:56,109
but he's really sweet on the phone.

1430
00:56:56,679 --> 00:56:58,909
- It's every three months. - Do you hear his voice?

1431
00:56:59,449 --> 00:57:01,549
There will be an X-ray scan and a CT scan.

1432
00:57:01,819 --> 00:57:02,879
What's wrong?

1433
00:57:03,379 --> 00:57:05,018
I will be checked...

1434
00:57:05,019 --> 00:57:07,518
for any issues in my body.

1435
00:57:07,519 --> 00:57:08,659
Gosh.

1436
00:57:08,859 --> 00:57:10,618
Their teeth are very sharp at that age.

1437
00:57:10,619 --> 00:57:11,779
- Right. - They hurt so much.

1438
00:57:13,059 --> 00:57:14,759
What was that? Gosh, that hurt!

1439
00:57:15,029 --> 00:57:16,398
Every three months...

1440
00:57:16,399 --> 00:57:18,528
- It bites your toes, doesn't it? - Right. It bit my toe.

1441
00:57:18,529 --> 00:57:19,568
(Groaning)

1442
00:57:19,569 --> 00:57:20,899
He knew right away.

1443
00:57:21,899 --> 00:57:23,698
It bites at you and runs around.

1444
00:57:23,699 --> 00:57:25,168
That's what it does.

1445
00:57:25,169 --> 00:57:26,309
- Right. - Is that so?

1446
00:57:26,509 --> 00:57:27,569
Right.

1447
00:57:27,809 --> 00:57:29,538
Gosh, its teeth must feel itchy.

1448
00:57:29,539 --> 00:57:30,608
Right.

1449
00:57:30,609 --> 00:57:32,609
The dog is biting everything. Gosh!

1450
00:57:33,649 --> 00:57:35,679
We should name the dog.

1451
00:57:35,749 --> 00:57:36,778
Right.

1452
00:57:36,779 --> 00:57:39,489
What should we call it? I thought of Sunmoo...

1453
00:57:39,889 --> 00:57:41,089
as it's white.

1454
00:57:41,249 --> 00:57:43,089
Sunmoo is a strange name.

1455
00:57:43,419 --> 00:57:45,189
What do you and Mom call it?

1456
00:57:45,559 --> 00:57:47,788
We call it Goofball because it's a ball of trouble.

1457
00:57:47,789 --> 00:57:48,959
Goofball?

1458
00:57:49,499 --> 00:57:50,958
Should we call it Goofball?

1459
00:57:50,959 --> 00:57:52,099
- Goofball! - Right.

1460
00:57:52,929 --> 00:57:53,929
How cute!

1461
00:57:54,369 --> 00:57:55,539
It's full of energy.

1462
00:57:55,839 --> 00:57:57,938
- Okay. I'll call you again. - Right.

1463
00:57:57,939 --> 00:57:59,039
- Bye. - Bye.

1464
00:58:00,369 --> 00:58:01,439
Gosh, that hurt!

1465
00:58:02,079 --> 00:58:04,339
(Biting again)

1466
00:58:05,709 --> 00:58:06,709
It has so much energy.

1467
00:58:07,109 --> 00:58:09,079
Bite him.

1468
00:58:09,349 --> 00:58:10,449
Kill him.

1469
00:58:10,979 --> 00:58:12,248
(Biting)

1470
00:58:12,249 --> 00:58:13,749
It only bites my pinky toe.

1471
00:58:13,949 --> 00:58:15,459
(Oh, no!)

1472
00:58:16,189 --> 00:58:19,459
(Target locked on Moomoo's legs)

1473
00:58:20,659 --> 00:58:22,675
- Gosh, your teeth... - Does it think it's a dog chew?

1474
00:58:22,699 --> 00:58:23,798
It must have a nice texture.

1475
00:58:23,799 --> 00:58:25,059
(Laughing)

1476
00:58:25,729 --> 00:58:27,098
(Someone help Fathermoo!)

1477
00:58:27,099 --> 00:58:29,138
It has to be trained at that age...

1478
00:58:29,139 --> 00:58:30,369
to avoid biting in the future.

1479
00:58:31,439 --> 00:58:33,639
It's full of energy. What a healthy dog.

1480
00:58:35,409 --> 00:58:37,139
Should I call it Nonsense?

1481
00:58:37,609 --> 00:58:39,479
(That's too harsh.)

1482
00:58:40,309 --> 00:58:42,519
Nonsense!

1483
00:58:43,879 --> 00:58:44,949
It doesn't like that name.

1484
00:58:46,319 --> 00:58:47,419
Yeolmoo?

1485
00:58:48,589 --> 00:58:49,658
Yeolmoo!

1486
00:58:49,659 --> 00:58:51,289
(It's so cute.)

1487
00:58:51,519 --> 00:58:53,829
- Altarimoo? - Altarimoo?

1488
00:58:53,989 --> 00:58:55,549
He's going for names that end with Moo.

1489
00:58:55,999 --> 00:58:57,758
Do you like Altarimoo?

1490
00:58:57,759 --> 00:58:58,969
Should we go with that name?

1491
00:58:59,169 --> 00:59:00,229
Altarimoo!

1492
00:59:00,399 --> 00:59:02,869
(Ignoring)

1493
00:59:03,299 --> 00:59:04,668
(Thinking)

1494
00:59:04,669 --> 00:59:07,439
Dogs should have a childish name.

1495
00:59:08,069 --> 00:59:09,138
Done.

1496
00:59:09,139 --> 00:59:10,939
(You've decided on a name?)

1497
00:59:11,639 --> 00:59:14,039
You'll be called Sun Moo when you go to places like the vet.

1498
00:59:14,179 --> 00:59:15,859
You'll be called Goofball at home. Got it?

1499
00:59:16,419 --> 00:59:17,649
You're Sunmoo now.

1500
00:59:18,279 --> 00:59:20,439
Your nickname is Goofball. The decision has been made.

1501
00:59:21,319 --> 00:59:23,159
Why is it Sunmoo?

1502
00:59:23,289 --> 00:59:24,589
- The dog is white. - Right.

1503
00:59:24,689 --> 00:59:26,088
I wanted the name to end with Moo,

1504
00:59:26,089 --> 00:59:27,689
- but Yeolmoo is too common. - Right.

1505
00:59:27,789 --> 00:59:29,759
I thought of Sunmoo as soon as I saw the dog.

1506
00:59:30,059 --> 00:59:31,659
- Jeon Sunmoo. - Jeon Sunmoo.

1507
00:59:32,629 --> 00:59:35,439
(Jeon Sunmoo, 70 days old)

1508
00:59:36,599 --> 00:59:37,739
Come here.

1509
00:59:37,939 --> 00:59:38,969
Sit.

1510
00:59:39,369 --> 00:59:40,539
Get up.

1511
00:59:41,269 --> 00:59:42,409
Get up.

1512
00:59:42,909 --> 00:59:44,378
(Lying down)

1513
00:59:44,379 --> 00:59:45,548
- It did the opposite. - It's so cute.

1514
00:59:45,549 --> 00:59:46,979
That's "down."

1515
00:59:47,649 --> 00:59:49,149
Come here, Sunmoo. Sit.

1516
00:59:50,479 --> 00:59:51,748
(Lying down)

1517
00:59:51,749 --> 00:59:53,648
(It's so cute.)

1518
00:59:53,649 --> 00:59:55,188
That's "down."

1519
00:59:55,189 --> 00:59:57,288
I told you to sit, ugly puppy.

1520
00:59:57,289 --> 00:59:58,959
- Time will fly like that. - Right.

1521
00:59:59,759 --> 01:00:01,228
Does Sunmoo not want to become president?

1522
01:00:01,229 --> 01:00:02,959
(Dalkong's brother keeps him in check.)

1523
01:00:03,259 --> 01:00:04,999
A dog that cute would become president.

1524
01:00:05,769 --> 01:00:07,529
(You're right about that.)

1525
01:00:07,999 --> 01:00:09,169
Get up.

1526
01:00:10,439 --> 01:00:11,699
(Like this!)

1527
01:00:12,609 --> 01:00:13,808
Sit, baby.

1528
01:00:13,809 --> 01:00:14,839
(Confused Sunmoo)

1529
01:00:15,069 --> 01:00:16,109
Paw!

1530
01:00:16,779 --> 01:00:17,839
Paw!

1531
01:00:18,309 --> 01:00:20,709
You give me your paw like this.

1532
01:00:21,079 --> 01:00:22,379
All right. Paw!

1533
01:00:22,919 --> 01:00:24,119
Like this.

1534
01:00:24,249 --> 01:00:25,278
Paw!

1535
01:00:25,279 --> 01:00:26,649
(Biting)

1536
01:00:26,919 --> 01:00:29,358
(A bite instead of its paw)

1537
01:00:29,359 --> 01:00:32,689
It will only get trained when there's a reward.

1538
01:00:33,129 --> 01:00:35,328
It doesn't like treats yet. It doesn't eat a lot yet.

1539
01:00:35,329 --> 01:00:36,729
Give the dog your toe.

1540
01:00:36,899 --> 01:00:38,359
Your toe will be the reward.

1541
01:00:38,629 --> 01:00:39,669
That's what I should do.

1542
01:00:40,369 --> 01:00:42,599
(I must do what I can to train the dog.)

1543
01:00:42,839 --> 01:00:44,269
I didn't tell you to bite me.

1544
01:00:44,439 --> 01:00:45,769
That's "bite."

1545
01:00:45,909 --> 01:00:46,938
Bite!

1546
01:00:46,939 --> 01:00:48,238
(Bite!)

1547
01:00:48,239 --> 01:00:49,308
(Licking)

1548
01:00:49,309 --> 01:00:50,439
That's "lick."

1549
01:00:51,679 --> 01:00:53,949
(He's all smiles even though it gets it wrong.)

1550
01:00:54,079 --> 01:00:55,479
High-five! Bam!

1551
01:00:55,819 --> 01:00:59,219
(He doesn't give up and continues with the training.)

1552
01:01:00,149 --> 01:01:01,189
"Sit."

1553
01:01:01,749 --> 01:01:02,789
"Down."

1554
01:01:03,289 --> 01:01:04,419
"Up."

1555
01:01:05,289 --> 01:01:06,328
There you go.

1556
01:01:06,329 --> 01:01:07,388
(I don't like studying!)

1557
01:01:07,389 --> 01:01:08,829
(Thinking)

1558
01:01:09,029 --> 01:01:10,829
That fellow won't become president.

1559
01:01:11,359 --> 01:01:12,699
It's already a competition.

1560
01:01:13,299 --> 01:01:15,028
It will be hard to secure a top position.

1561
01:01:15,029 --> 01:01:16,669
(Dalkong's father is just as passionate.)

1562
01:01:16,969 --> 01:01:18,909
(This won't work.)

1563
01:01:19,109 --> 01:01:21,609
Come here! Let's go for a walk!

1564
01:01:23,539 --> 01:01:24,608
Let's go for a walk!

1565
01:01:24,609 --> 01:01:25,649
(A walk?)

1566
01:01:25,779 --> 01:01:26,849
Sunmoo!

1567
01:01:27,709 --> 01:01:29,019
Come here, Sunmoo!

1568
01:01:29,719 --> 01:01:30,978
